WEBVTT

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:28.260
Shōgakukan, Inc.
Yomiuri Telecasting Corporation
Nippon Television Network
Shōgakukan Productions Co., Ltd.
Tōhō Co., Ltd.
TMS Entertainment, Ltd.

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:28.260
'Detective Conan' Production Committee

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:28.260
Produced by

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:28.260
.

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:35.640
Original Comic Books     Gōshō Aoyama
Serialised in Shōgakukan's 'Weekly Shōnen Sunday'

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:35.640
.

00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:46.150
.

00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:46.150
Screenplay   Takeharu Sakurai

00:00:55.540 --> 00:00:57.910
It can't be! That's a...

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:00.950
This is serious!

00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:04.930
This is an urgent call from Kurata to the Wakasa Coast Guard!

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:09.440
While on patrol, I found a boat containing explosives rigged to blow it up by the rockface near the fourth district!

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:14.340
And now for the news.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:19.520
The suspicious boat spotted in Maizuru Bay by the Coast Guard contained data and components not found in Japan...

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:25.660
It is believed to have entered the country illegally, and will undergo further investigation.

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:21.980
This is Maizuru Bay, isn't it?

00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:22.900
Yeah.

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:24.220
Did something happen?

00:01:24.220 --> 00:01:25.660
What is it?

00:01:25.660 --> 00:01:28.850
A suspicious boat was spotted on the coast this morning.

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:30.940
What's a suspicious boat?

00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:35.890
Hey, brats! Move up, don't leave a gap in the line!

00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:37.120
Right...

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:38.610
Come on, Dad!

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:41.750
You're the adult here, you're supposed to be watching the kids!

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:43.760
Oh, shut up.

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:46.630
I'm only here because you said somebody needed to come with you.

00:01:46.630 --> 00:01:50.090
But it's so rare to get a chance to go aboard an Aegis Destroyer!

00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:53.200
Getting tickets for one is ten times harder than for other ships!

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:56.340
If only you used that luck with the horses.

00:01:56.340 --> 00:01:56.800
Geez!

00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:00.260
Geez, the old man's rude wherever he goes...

00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:03.040
What is an Aegis Destroyer anyway?

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:05.050
Umm...

00:02:05.050 --> 00:02:11.230
Aegis Destroyers are warships fitted with a weapons system developed by the US Navy!

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:13.250
They're really strong warships!

00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:13.820
Yeah!

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:16.570
That's a pretty simple description.

00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:18.410
Are you even interested in warships, Ayumi-<i>chan</i>?

00:02:18.410 --> 00:02:19.730
No.

00:02:19.730 --> 00:02:22.820
But I love the sea, and we <i>did</i> win the tickets.

00:02:22.820 --> 00:02:24.110
That's right!

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:26.210
It's a once-in-a-lifetime experience!

00:02:26.210 --> 00:02:27.760
This transmission...

00:02:26.210 --> 00:02:28.770
So just forget about horses for now, Dad!

00:02:28.770 --> 00:02:30.600
Okay, okay!

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:31.670
Conan-<i>kun</i>?

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:33.180
I gotta go to the toilet.

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:34.790
Well, be quick.

00:02:34.790 --> 00:02:36.670
We'll be boarding soon.

00:02:36.670 --> 00:02:37.470
Sure!

00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:46.640
What's up, Doc?

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:51.360
Oh, I just wanted to see if your
 new satellite phone was working.

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:54.320
We haven't boarded the ship yet, let alone set sail.

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:58.240
Huh, they must really be taking a long time.

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:02.620
Yeah, they probably increased the security checks with the commotion about the suspicious boat today.

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:04.270
I see...

00:03:04.270 --> 00:03:09.040
Even though you made it just for the trip,
I might be better off not using the satellite phone.

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:12.340
By the way, did that conference in Ōsaka go well?

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:15.790
Yeah, thanks to Ai-<i>kun</i>'s help.

00:03:15.790 --> 00:03:17.300
We got great ratings.


00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:21.840
I see. Then how about we meet up after the public exercises are over?

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:23.120
I better get back to the line—

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:24.480
By the way...

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:28.480
The kids must be getting bored, waiting so long.

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:29.470
No, not really...

00:03:29.470 --> 00:03:31.640
All right, here's a quiz for them!

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:34.110
<i>That's</i> why you called me, huh?

00:03:34.570 --> 00:03:38.820
The 'Aegis' in 'Aegis Destroyer' comes from the name of the shield to drive away evil

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:44.590
that Zeus gave to his daughter Athena in Greek myth, as I'm sure you know.


00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:51.520
When Zeus fought the demonic Hydra, its sharp fangs are said to have bit him everywhere on his body.

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:54.570
However, there was one place he wasn't bitten.

00:03:54.570 --> 00:03:56.210
Where do you think it was?

00:03:56.210 --> 00:03:58.170
1. His neck.

00:03:58.170 --> 00:04:00.130
2. His chest.

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:02.090
3. His stomach.

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:04.100
4. His back.

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:05.640
And that's that.

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:09.060
The doc really wanted me to have you answer it.

00:04:10.460 --> 00:04:14.060
Wait, Conan-<i>kun</i>, when did you talk to the doctor?

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:17.330
Huh? Oh, when I was just in the toilet.

00:04:17.330 --> 00:04:19.410
Hey, Conan-<i>kun</i>, I can't solve it.

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:20.390
Me neither!

00:04:20.390 --> 00:04:21.410
What's the answer?

00:04:21.410 --> 00:04:23.650
The answer is number four — his back.

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:24.690
How come?

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:27.020
It's the ‘god's back’, so it ‘wasn't bitten’.

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:27.020
kami nokoshi

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:27.020
kami no koshi

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:29.840
Just another pun, huh?!

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:33.390
Would the next group please get their winning postcard ready and come forward.

00:04:33.390 --> 00:04:35.360
Oh, our turn's finally here!

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:36.590
Yay!

00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:39.110
I'm tired of waiting!

00:04:39.110 --> 00:04:41.470
Hey! Don't run!

00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:48.690
Please open any hand luggage you may have so it can be checked, and place it in front of one of the inspectors.

00:04:48.690 --> 00:04:54.480
Also, mobile phones are not allowed aboard, so we will hold onto them for you here.

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:58.440
Aegis Destroyer Hotaka

00:05:31.220 --> 00:05:36.440
Thank you for joining us on these public exercises aboard an Aegis Destroyer.

00:05:36.740 --> 00:05:41.320
My name is Inoue, and I'll be your guide today.

00:05:37.650 --> 00:05:41.610
Chief Navigator of the Hotaka

00:05:37.650 --> 00:05:41.610
Lt. Commander Fumitada Inoue

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:42.780
It's a pleasure to have you here.

00:05:44.090 --> 00:05:48.410
I'll start by explaining the
 details for today's public exercises.

00:05:48.410 --> 00:05:51.900
First, please look at the map on the front screen.

00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:56.660
You're free to look around the sections marked in red.

00:05:56.660 --> 00:05:59.880
However, please avoid going into
 any other corridors and rooms.

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:03.720
You'll find further details on the pamphlets in front of you.

00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:07.600
Next, I'll talk about the schedule for today...

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:08.300
Sonoko...

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:14.070
{0-ji chōdo, kochira no shokudō de kaijōjieitai no shōkai eizō o 15-fun hodo miteitadakimasu.}At noon precisely, we have a roughly 15-minute video showcasing the Japan Maritime Self-Defence Force for you to watch.

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:08.760
Huh?

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:09.720
What time is it?

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:11.350
Let's see...

00:06:11.350 --> 00:06:12.680
Ran-<i>neechan</i>, where's your watch?

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:15.650
It broke, so I sent it to be repaired.

00:06:14.070 --> 00:06:18.600
{tsuzuite 0-ji 20-fun, kyūmeidōi no setsumei o shimasu.}Afterward, at 12:20, I'll explain to you how to use lifejackets.

00:06:15.650 --> 00:06:19.100
I'd been using my mobile phone in the meantime, but...

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:23.180
{kampan ni deru toki wa, mina-san, kochira o kanarazu chakuyōshitemoraimasu.}When out on deck, please make sure to always wear one of these.

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:20.810
You can't because it was confiscated.

00:06:20.810 --> 00:06:23.900
If you want to, you can use my watch.

00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:27.740
{shūgōjikan o mamotte kudasai.}The deck is a very dangerous place while we are at sea, so please follow any orders you may be given,

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:26.770
Huh? But what about you, Mitsuhiko-<i>kun</i>?

00:06:26.770 --> 00:06:29.870
My digital camera has a clock, so I'll be fine.

00:06:27.740 --> 00:06:29.870
{shūgōjikan o mamotte kudasai.}and remember the set gathering times.

00:06:29.870 --> 00:06:33.200
{iin desu ka? fune wa jikan genshu desu.}Got it? Keeping time is very important while aboard a ship.

00:06:32.570 --> 00:06:33.730
You heard him.

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:39.830
{soshite 0-ji 40-pun, honjitsu no medama, taikūsentō no yōjō kunren o okonaimasu.}Then at 12:40, we'll be holding the main event of the day, anti-air training exercises at sea.

00:06:33.730 --> 00:06:34.690
Why say no?

00:06:34.690 --> 00:06:35.330
Yeah.

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:37.700
Thank you, then, Mitsuhiko-<i>kun</i>.

00:06:37.700 --> 00:06:38.310
Sure.

00:06:38.310 --> 00:06:41.880
It's completely waterproof, so you don't have to worry about the sea breeze.

00:06:39.830 --> 00:06:46.120
{13-ji, kampan ni dete kakushu heiki ya radar, tōsai heli nado no kengaku o okonaimasu.}At 13:00, you can head out onto the deck, and observe the various weapons and radars, and the on-board helicopter.

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:45.110
And it's a radio clock, so it's very accurate.

00:06:45.110 --> 00:06:46.590
What's a radio clock?

00:06:46.120 --> 00:06:53.680
{sono ato, 16-ji 30-pun, mina-san ni kaijōjieitai no meibutsu, kaigun curry o tabeteitadakimasu.}After that, at 16:30, you all can enjoy the JMSDF specialty, Navy Curry.

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:48.220
You don't know?

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:52.690
It's a clock that sets itself several times a day according to radio signals transmitting the correct time.

00:06:52.690 --> 00:06:53.680
Wow...

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:57.140
Incidentally, that one sets itself at 5:00 AM and 5:00 PM.

00:06:53.680 --> 00:07:01.120
{o-shokuji no ato, kan'nai no shokudō to kampan ni kakusareta takarasagashi game o okonaimasu no de, otanoshimi ni.}After the meal, we'll be holding a treasure hunt for items hidden in the cafeteria and on deck, so look forward to that.

00:06:57.140 --> 00:06:59.470
Where do the signals come from?

00:06:59.470 --> 00:07:00.690
Uh, well...

00:07:00.690 --> 00:07:03.680
Around here, it'd probably be the transmitter in Fukushima.

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:05.870
{game o shiteiru aida ni, honkan wa futatabi maizuru-kō o mezashite susumimasu.}During the game, we'll be heading back to Maizuru Harbour.

00:07:03.680 --> 00:07:04.690
Really?

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:06.940
You sure know a lot, don't you, Conan-<i>kun</i>?

00:07:05.870 --> 00:07:09.790
{minato e no tōchaku jikoku wa, 17-ji 30-pun no yotei desu.}We expect to arrive back at the harbour at 17:30.

00:07:06.940 --> 00:07:09.890
O-Oh, I heard about it from Shin'ichi-<i>niichan</i>...

00:07:09.890 --> 00:07:11.490
Huh? What's that?!

00:07:11.490 --> 00:07:12.530
What?

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:13.830
What's that creepy sound?

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:16.180
What? What happened?

00:07:16.180 --> 00:07:17.450
Please calm down.

00:07:17.450 --> 00:07:18.620
Everything's fine.

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:18.960
Huh?

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:24.800
The sound you just heard was made by our pumping system letting in a large amount of sea water.

00:07:24.800 --> 00:07:27.300
Hey, Dad!

00:07:24.800 --> 00:07:27.300
Please calm down and sit down.

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:28.380
Oh, and...

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:32.890
It seems the pump valve in your
 mouth came loose, so be careful.

00:07:34.280 --> 00:07:36.220
Oh, sorry, sorry.

00:07:36.220 --> 00:07:37.090
Dad!

00:07:37.090 --> 00:07:38.950
Sit down, I'm begging you!

00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:41.950
Geez...

00:07:41.950 --> 00:07:48.410
Since the pumping system started up, we may be about to leave Maizuru Harbour.

00:07:42.540 --> 00:07:46.230
But would a pumping system really make a sound like that?

00:08:13.210 --> 00:08:16.310
I'm Shin'ichi Kudō, a high school detective.

00:08:16.310 --> 00:08:19.860
While at an amusement park with my childhood friend and classmate, Ran Mouri,

00:08:19.860 --> 00:08:24.310
I witnessed a suspicious deal involving a man in black.

00:08:24.310 --> 00:08:29.610
Since I was so focused on watching the deal, I didn't realise his partner was sneaking up from behind me.


00:08:32.450 --> 00:08:37.580
He forced me to consume poison, and when I came to...

00:08:37.580 --> 00:08:40.050
...my body had shrunk!

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:43.460
If those men learnt that Shin'ichi Kudō was still alive,

00:08:43.460 --> 00:08:46.840
they'd come back to finish me off, endangering everyone around me.

00:08:47.230 --> 00:08:50.760
At Dr. Agasa's suggestion, I hid my identity,

00:08:50.760 --> 00:08:54.510
and when Ran asked my name,
 I blurted out ‘Conan Edogawa’.

00:08:55.090 --> 00:09:00.130
To find out more about those guys, I ended up living with Ran and her detective father.

00:09:02.160 --> 00:09:04.520
These are my classmates now...

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:05.770
Genta.

00:09:05.770 --> 00:09:06.650
Mitsuhiko.

00:09:06.650 --> 00:09:07.320
Ayumi.

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:12.780
They formed the Detective Boys, and forced me to join.

00:09:12.780 --> 00:09:16.780
And this old man is Kogorō Mouri.

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:26.070
I don't have to explain that, right?

00:09:26.070 --> 00:09:29.000
These two gadgets were made by Dr. Agasa.

00:09:29.320 --> 00:09:34.400
He makes all sorts of unique gadgets for my vertically challenged body.

00:09:34.400 --> 00:09:36.010
The Instant Football Belt.

00:09:36.010 --> 00:09:40.700
When you press the button on the buckle, a ball pops out — pretty nifty.

00:09:41.640 --> 00:09:46.100
And the main focus this time is on this watch, and its new functions.

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:49.070
It has a satellite phone and a USB flash drive built-in.

00:09:49.070 --> 00:09:52.030
Now that it's powered up, it's <i>really</i> nifty!

00:09:52.990 --> 00:09:57.870
By the way, the doc isn't the
 only one who knows my identity.

00:09:58.270 --> 00:09:59.990
Ai Haibara.

00:09:59.990 --> 00:10:02.370
Real name: Shiho Miyano.

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:06.310
She used to be with the men in black,

00:10:06.310 --> 00:10:12.280
but to get away from them, she took the same drug that'd been forced on me, and ended up shrinking.

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:20.640
Haibara came to live with the doc, and joined me as a first-year primary school student.

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:24.600
My body shrunk, but my mind didn't!

00:10:24.960 --> 00:10:26.770
I'm still an undefeated great detective!

00:10:27.910 --> 00:10:32.780
There's always only one truth!

00:10:40.850 --> 00:10:43.120
Prepare for anti-air combat drill!

00:10:44.910 --> 00:10:46.370
All units in position.

00:10:46.370 --> 00:10:48.500
This ship will now enter anti-air combat.

00:10:49.080 --> 00:10:51.370
All hands, hurry to your positions!

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:55.400
If you have children with you, please come to the front.

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:57.550
We will now perform a publicly observed combat drill.

00:10:55.400 --> 00:10:59.180
There's not much space, so if you're in the front line, please stay behind this point.

00:10:57.550 --> 00:10:59.180
Keep a close eye on the sky!

00:10:59.180 --> 00:11:03.340
This is the heart of an Aegis Destroyer, the CIC.

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:02.310
Anti-air radar ready!

00:11:02.310 --> 00:11:04.420
SPY detected a target! 40°, 70 miles.

00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:05.390
Target #1 approaching!

00:11:05.390 --> 00:11:08.290
35°, 66 miles.

00:11:06.420 --> 00:11:08.290
Is it coming here?

00:11:08.290 --> 00:11:10.020
That's just how it's set up...

00:11:10.020 --> 00:11:11.180
I see.

00:11:11.180 --> 00:11:13.530
Oh... Don't scare me like that.

00:11:13.530 --> 00:11:16.100
They seem to be taking it quite lightly...

00:11:16.100 --> 00:11:19.300
New target detected! 30°, 40 miles.

00:11:16.100 --> 00:11:19.300
Yeah, they're not acting too well...

00:11:19.300 --> 00:11:22.080
Designated as target #2.

00:11:19.300 --> 00:11:22.080
Ain't that because this is the real thing?

00:11:22.080 --> 00:11:25.410
Target #2 is heading straight for us.

00:11:25.410 --> 00:11:28.260
Target #2 is determined to be a threat.

00:11:28.260 --> 00:11:29.540
Prepare to attack immediately!

00:11:30.070 --> 00:11:33.170
Anti-air combat drill target designated by CIC.

00:11:33.170 --> 00:11:34.700
Begin attack!

00:11:34.700 --> 00:11:36.010
Prepare the main gun!

00:11:36.260 --> 00:11:39.260
Prepare to fire the Mark 45 Mod 4.

00:11:39.260 --> 00:11:42.140
Remote aiming at target #2 complete.

00:11:42.140 --> 00:11:44.460
The target has entered the firing range.

00:11:44.460 --> 00:11:45.720
Prepare to fire!

00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:48.060
Begin firing procedure!

00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:48.810
Fire!

00:11:49.240 --> 00:11:51.550
30 seconds to target.

00:11:52.280 --> 00:11:54.980
Huh, it's just images on a screen...?

00:11:54.980 --> 00:11:56.480
Come on, Dad...

00:11:56.480 --> 00:11:58.860
Even just watching a screen in here is impressive...

00:11:59.180 --> 00:12:04.200
This is an Aegis Destroyer's most confidential room — it's the first time civilians have been allowed to be here.

00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:07.950
I guess it <i>does</i> give off that feel of secrecy...

00:12:08.650 --> 00:12:10.920
Target #2 hit.

00:12:10.920 --> 00:12:12.500
It's like some sort of game!

00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:13.630
Target #2 confirmed to be hit.

00:12:14.060 --> 00:12:16.540
Do you think they'll let us have a go too?

00:12:16.540 --> 00:12:18.470
Not in a million years.

00:12:18.470 --> 00:12:21.430
He's right! It may look easy, but...

00:12:18.940 --> 00:12:21.430
Hey, hey, not you guys too...

00:12:21.430 --> 00:12:22.760
Ready to fire!

00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:24.300
Fire!

00:12:24.300 --> 00:12:25.460
Automatic mode!

00:12:25.460 --> 00:12:27.000
Mark intercepted!

00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:28.980
Target #1 is descending!

00:12:29.700 --> 00:12:32.070
12 seconds to target #1.

00:12:33.300 --> 00:12:35.310
Target #1 hit!

00:12:35.940 --> 00:12:37.880
What happened, did it hit?

00:12:37.880 --> 00:12:41.650
Yes, with that, all of the enemies were shot down.

00:12:41.650 --> 00:12:43.890
Wasn't that great?

00:12:43.890 --> 00:12:44.590
Yeah!

00:12:44.590 --> 00:12:45.380
It's already over?

00:12:45.380 --> 00:12:47.370
I couldn't quite tell what was going on...

00:12:48.560 --> 00:12:51.050
That's all for—

00:12:49.640 --> 00:12:51.830
There's a sonar response! Nationality unknown!

00:12:51.830 --> 00:12:53.790
Beginning search for target <i>α</i>!

00:12:54.330 --> 00:12:56.170
It's heading straight for us!

00:12:56.650 --> 00:12:57.840
Target <i>α</i>!

00:12:57.840 --> 00:12:58.640
Direction: 5°.

00:12:58.640 --> 00:12:59.940
Distance: 8000!

00:12:59.940 --> 00:13:00.970
This is the CIC!

00:13:00.970 --> 00:13:03.500
Target <i>α</i> detected! Direction: 5°. Distance: 8000!

00:13:03.500 --> 00:13:04.860
Did you say Target <i>α</i>?!

00:13:04.860 --> 00:13:05.860
Captain...

00:13:07.430 --> 00:13:08.810
This is your captain, Tateishi.

00:13:08.810 --> 00:13:12.810
Capt. Yukio Tateishi

00:13:08.810 --> 00:13:12.810
Captain of the Hotaka

00:13:08.810 --> 00:13:12.140
Begin search with all radars.

00:13:12.140 --> 00:13:14.080
I'll head to the CIC.

00:13:14.080 --> 00:13:15.450
I'll come with you.

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:18.970
I'm going to the CIC.

00:13:18.970 --> 00:13:21.530
I leave the vice-captain in command of the bridge.

00:13:21.530 --> 00:13:25.070
Target <i>α</i> is maintaining its course straight towards us!

00:13:25.070 --> 00:13:26.050
Roger.

00:13:26.050 --> 00:13:28.110
Be ready for any change in course or speed from the target!

00:13:28.110 --> 00:13:30.020
 Be ready for any attack from the target.

00:13:30.020 --> 00:13:32.620
It is not an animal or a natural phenomenon!

00:13:32.620 --> 00:13:34.960
No response to IFF signals!

00:13:35.960 --> 00:13:38.040
It's a submerged, non-allied ship!

00:13:38.640 --> 00:13:41.380
Start the Nixie! Stop the ship!

00:13:41.380 --> 00:13:44.240
Full speed astern! Hard a-port!

00:13:44.240 --> 00:13:45.780
Aim the bow towards the target.

00:13:45.780 --> 00:13:46.670
Roger.

00:13:46.670 --> 00:13:48.010
Full speed astern!

00:13:48.010 --> 00:13:51.140
Hard a-port! Pivot by 90°!

00:13:53.910 --> 00:13:55.830
Did the ship actually stop?

00:13:55.830 --> 00:13:58.450
Looks like the performance suddenly got a lot more realistic!

00:13:58.450 --> 00:14:00.280
Yeah, it's really intense.

00:14:00.280 --> 00:14:02.690
Prepare for anti-submarine combat!
 Send out a warning signal!

00:14:02.690 --> 00:14:03.760
Roger!

00:14:03.760 --> 00:14:04.590
Signal ready.

00:14:04.590 --> 00:14:06.530
Warning signal fired!

00:14:11.870 --> 00:14:13.900
Showing it on the third main monitor!

00:14:14.660 --> 00:14:15.790
Amazing!

00:14:15.790 --> 00:14:16.800
That was so cool!

00:14:16.800 --> 00:14:17.540
Yeah!

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:18.820
Wasn't that cool?

00:14:18.820 --> 00:14:20.590
I wonder if that light was the real thing?

00:14:20.590 --> 00:14:21.890
No way...!

00:14:21.890 --> 00:14:23.880
Prepare for anti-submarine combat!

00:14:24.410 --> 00:14:25.760
Red alert!

00:14:27.060 --> 00:14:28.260
Aye, sir!

00:14:28.260 --> 00:14:33.930
The ship may shake slightly, so if you have children with you, be sure to keep an eye on them.

00:14:29.950 --> 00:14:33.930
Have Ichigaya check the data against nearby submarines.

00:14:33.930 --> 00:14:36.080
Did something happen?

00:14:36.080 --> 00:14:37.850
This is just training, right?

00:14:37.850 --> 00:14:38.900
Of course it is!

00:14:39.220 --> 00:14:41.670
They just finally spiced it up a bit!

00:14:41.670 --> 00:14:43.860
No, this might actually be...

00:14:43.860 --> 00:14:45.390
The echo is dull.

00:14:45.390 --> 00:14:46.270
What's the situation?

00:14:46.270 --> 00:14:48.000
The image quality isn't clear.

00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:49.820
It's not good enough for detection.

00:14:50.220 --> 00:14:51.980
Stop the SPY!

00:14:51.980 --> 00:14:54.770
Confirm target with the SH-60K!

00:14:54.770 --> 00:14:56.020
Target still approaching!

00:14:57.580 --> 00:14:59.280
Distance: 3,200 metres!

00:14:59.290 --> 00:15:01.130
We'll be in the target's torpedo range soon!

00:15:01.130 --> 00:15:02.240
What?!

00:15:02.810 --> 00:15:04.090
Still no response from the target?

00:15:04.850 --> 00:15:05.940
 Negative.

00:15:05.940 --> 00:15:07.740
Target still approaching!

00:15:07.740 --> 00:15:09.390
Distance: 3,100 metres!

00:15:09.390 --> 00:15:12.480
Only 100 metres left before we're in torpedo range!

00:15:12.480 --> 00:15:13.430
Captain...

00:15:13.830 --> 00:15:15.350
What should we do?

00:15:17.230 --> 00:15:19.060
All hands, prepare for an ambush!

00:15:19.890 --> 00:15:21.270
Hold on, Captain!

00:15:21.270 --> 00:15:22.720
If you do that...

00:15:22.720 --> 00:15:24.110
We might start a war.

00:15:24.980 --> 00:15:27.490
Target speed: 10! Distance: 3,000!

00:15:27.820 --> 00:15:30.200
We're in the target's firing range!

00:15:30.200 --> 00:15:32.660
Maintain a distance of 3,000 metres from the target.

00:15:32.870 --> 00:15:34.910
Start the engines at full speed!

00:15:34.910 --> 00:15:35.720
Roger!

00:15:35.720 --> 00:15:37.800
Starting engines at full speed!

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:40.100
Take evasive manoeuvres!

00:15:40.100 --> 00:15:42.710
Hard a-starboard! Full speed ahead!

00:15:48.330 --> 00:15:50.440
It feels so tense in here!

00:15:50.440 --> 00:15:52.540
It's even better than a game!

00:15:52.540 --> 00:15:54.010
It's a bit scary.

00:15:54.330 --> 00:15:57.030
It's no surprise that they're scared.

00:15:57.030 --> 00:15:58.580
This Aegis Destroyer...

00:15:58.580 --> 00:16:00.900
...really <i>is</i> being attacked!

00:16:02.360 --> 00:16:03.860
No response from the target.

00:16:03.860 --> 00:16:05.240
Approaching at a 40° angle from the left.

00:16:05.240 --> 00:16:07.570
I want to see the enemy. Prepare light torpedoes!

00:16:07.570 --> 00:16:09.340
Light torpedoes ready!

00:16:09.340 --> 00:16:11.410
Engines to full power! Hard a-port!

00:16:11.410 --> 00:16:13.350
Anti-submarine light torpedoes ready!

00:16:13.350 --> 00:16:16.620
CIC to the bridge, engines to full power! Hard a-port!

00:16:16.620 --> 00:16:19.080
Full speed ahead! Hard a-port!

00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:21.170
Hard a-port!

00:16:28.760 --> 00:16:30.220
This is the left torpedo launcher.

00:16:30.660 --> 00:16:32.780
Anti-submarine torpedo loaded!

00:16:32.780 --> 00:16:33.930
Launch torpedo!

00:16:33.930 --> 00:16:36.140
Fire anti-submarine light torpedo!

00:16:53.950 --> 00:16:57.140
 We'll have a clear visual soon!
 Showing it on the third monitor!

00:16:59.020 --> 00:17:00.410
Shockwave incoming!

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:01.850
The ship will shake slightly.

00:17:01.850 --> 00:17:03.710
 Make sure to keep an eye on your children!

00:17:11.630 --> 00:17:13.670
Hey, are you guys okay?

00:17:13.670 --> 00:17:14.480
Yeah.

00:17:14.480 --> 00:17:16.250
That shake was awesome!

00:17:16.250 --> 00:17:17.970
It was so cool!

00:17:17.970 --> 00:17:20.160
Huh? That kid doesn't have any adult with him.

00:17:20.160 --> 00:17:21.560
What's that?!

00:17:21.560 --> 00:17:22.970
A submarine?

00:17:22.970 --> 00:17:24.480
No, that's not it.

00:17:25.400 --> 00:17:26.680
A fishing boat?

00:17:26.680 --> 00:17:27.610
A shipwreck?

00:17:28.250 --> 00:17:29.480
Is that...

00:17:29.720 --> 00:17:32.200
No risk of explosion.

00:17:32.680 --> 00:17:35.910
It's a shipwreck drifting with the tide...

00:17:38.980 --> 00:17:41.000
Cease use of anti-submarine weapons!

00:17:41.960 --> 00:17:43.870
Cease use of anti-submarine weapons!

00:17:44.300 --> 00:17:47.420
Now returning to the route planned for the public exercises.

00:17:47.420 --> 00:17:52.100
I repeat, now returning to the route planned for the public exercises.

00:17:52.100 --> 00:17:54.810
Notify US Navy and SDF submarines that we have ceased combat...

00:17:54.810 --> 00:17:56.550
Is it over?

00:17:57.410 --> 00:18:02.500
Yes, that's the end of the anti-air and anti-submarine combat training.

00:18:03.140 --> 00:18:04.950
Wasn't that amazing?

00:18:04.950 --> 00:18:05.490
Yeah!

00:18:05.490 --> 00:18:07.620
I thought it was a real fight!

00:18:07.620 --> 00:18:09.730
I even forgot I was hungry!

00:18:09.890 --> 00:18:12.610
So they're just calling it training...

00:18:18.870 --> 00:18:21.860
Well then, please enjoy looking around the bow.

00:18:21.860 --> 00:18:22.880
Sure!

00:18:24.540 --> 00:18:26.770
Isn't the SDF cool?

00:18:26.770 --> 00:18:28.980
I want to try on an SDF uniform!

00:18:28.980 --> 00:18:29.500
It's so cool!

00:18:29.500 --> 00:18:32.000
Conan-<i>kun</i>, hurry up, hurry up!

00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:34.450
This Aegis Destroyer's really big!

00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:34.450
This cannon's amazing!{Sonoko}

00:18:34.450 --> 00:18:36.980
I wonder how big it really is.

00:18:34.450 --> 00:18:38.020
It really feels huge when you see it close up...{Ran}

00:18:38.020 --> 00:18:41.470
We saw it being fired on that video earlier.

00:18:41.470 --> 00:18:44.180
Conan-<i>kun</i>, let's take a photo with all of us together!

00:18:44.180 --> 00:18:45.600
S-Sure!

00:18:45.600 --> 00:18:47.270
Over here!

00:18:47.270 --> 00:18:49.060
Let's go, Yūki.

00:18:49.060 --> 00:18:51.680
 Come on, take my hand, Yūki.

00:18:49.710 --> 00:18:51.680
Unless I'm mistaken, that kid...

00:18:54.470 --> 00:18:55.320
Hey!

00:18:55.320 --> 00:18:57.360
Is your name Yūki-<i>kun</i>?

00:18:57.360 --> 00:18:58.910
Huh? Yeah.

00:18:58.910 --> 00:19:00.240
What a relief, huh?

00:19:00.240 --> 00:19:01.780
You managed to find your dad!

00:19:02.480 --> 00:19:04.870
What do you mean, little kid?

00:19:04.870 --> 00:19:09.000
You weren't with him when the ship shook, right?

00:19:09.210 --> 00:19:11.200
I was worried about him.

00:19:11.200 --> 00:19:13.630
Oh, that must've been when I was in the toilet.

00:19:14.020 --> 00:19:16.340
Oh, so that's what happened...

00:19:17.220 --> 00:19:19.300
So you were all alone then, right?

00:19:19.300 --> 00:19:22.290
Well then, let's have a look at the other side, Yūki.

00:19:22.290 --> 00:19:23.070
Okay.

00:19:24.820 --> 00:19:28.480
Even if he was in the toilet, he should've felt a shake that big.

00:19:28.480 --> 00:19:36.320
But even after the drill in the CIC ended, he didn't show himself until the free time on the deck had already begun.

00:19:36.320 --> 00:19:37.960
I wonder...

00:19:39.590 --> 00:19:40.630
Hey!

00:19:40.630 --> 00:19:42.740
Don't go wandering off!

00:19:42.740 --> 00:19:43.460
Geez...

00:19:43.460 --> 00:19:46.160
You vanish as soon as I take my eyes off you!

00:19:46.540 --> 00:19:48.680
I'm sorry...

00:19:49.580 --> 00:19:52.130
A female SDF member on an Aegis Destroyer?

00:19:52.130 --> 00:19:53.410
Hey, brat!

00:19:53.410 --> 00:19:54.590
Are you really sorry?

00:19:54.590 --> 00:19:56.990
Oh, how cool!

00:19:56.990 --> 00:19:57.370
Huh?

00:19:57.370 --> 00:19:59.240
It's a female SDF member!

00:19:59.240 --> 00:19:59.970
Huh?!

00:20:01.200 --> 00:20:04.010
It's rare to see female SDF members, so let's get a group photo with her!

00:20:04.010 --> 00:20:05.280
It's true!

00:20:05.280 --> 00:20:06.290
She's beautiful!

00:20:06.290 --> 00:20:07.860
Let's do it, let's do it!

00:20:07.860 --> 00:20:08.940
Hey!

00:20:08.940 --> 00:20:12.900
Miss SDF member, can we take a photo with you?

00:20:12.900 --> 00:20:15.860
Captain

00:20:12.900 --> 00:20:15.860
Nanami Fujii

00:20:12.900 --> 00:20:14.250
A-A photo?

00:20:14.250 --> 00:20:15.860
What a beauty!

00:20:15.860 --> 00:20:19.860
A great detective and a beautiful SDF member. Miracles can happen!

00:20:20.180 --> 00:20:21.470
Miss!

00:20:21.470 --> 00:20:27.390
No, divine devotee to the SDF, please pay no mind to the bad manners of these children.

00:20:28.190 --> 00:20:29.590
Hey, Dad!

00:20:29.590 --> 00:20:32.830
What? I was about to ask her
 if we could take a photo with her!

00:20:32.830 --> 00:20:34.680
You don't have to get <i>that</i> close to her to do it!

00:20:34.680 --> 00:20:36.760
Mitsuhiko, can I borrow your camera?

00:20:36.760 --> 00:20:37.760
Huh? Okay.

00:20:37.760 --> 00:20:38.830
Thanks.

00:20:41.010 --> 00:20:42.800
Okay, everyone look this way!

00:20:44.440 --> 00:20:45.720
But I don't...

00:20:45.720 --> 00:20:47.730
You don't mind if we take a photo, right?

00:20:47.730 --> 00:20:48.600
Just look around!

00:20:48.600 --> 00:20:50.720
Take a photo of us this time!

00:20:50.720 --> 00:20:52.970
Am I doing the salute right?

00:20:53.610 --> 00:20:55.470
Well, I guess you're right...

00:20:55.470 --> 00:20:56.360
All right!

00:20:56.360 --> 00:20:57.560
I'll go next to her!

00:20:57.560 --> 00:20:58.970
I want to be next to her!

00:20:58.970 --> 00:21:00.510
Me too, me too!

00:21:00.510 --> 00:21:02.430
Conan-<i>kun</i>, are you okay with not being in the photo?

00:21:02.430 --> 00:21:03.060
It's fine.

00:21:03.060 --> 00:21:05.500
Anyway, you should move closer too, Ran-<i>neechan</i>.

00:21:05.500 --> 00:21:06.480
Right.

00:21:07.080 --> 00:21:09.260
Okay, I'm taking it!

00:21:09.790 --> 00:21:11.310
Oh, sorry...

00:21:11.310 --> 00:21:12.330
One more time!

00:21:12.330 --> 00:21:13.280
Huh?

00:21:13.280 --> 00:21:15.780
Hey, do you know how to take a photo?

00:21:15.780 --> 00:21:17.920
Yeah, but it was set up wrong.

00:21:17.920 --> 00:21:19.910
Okay, now it's perfect!

00:21:19.910 --> 00:21:21.130
Okay, this time...

00:21:21.130 --> 00:21:22.850
Say ‘Aegis’!

00:21:22.850 --> 00:21:24.360
Yay!

00:21:24.360 --> 00:21:25.150
How was it?

00:21:25.150 --> 00:21:26.020
Did you take it?

00:21:26.020 --> 00:21:27.750
Yup! It was perfect this time.

00:21:27.750 --> 00:21:29.100
Let me see, let me see!

00:21:29.100 --> 00:21:30.790
Thank you.

00:21:30.250 --> 00:21:30.790
Here!

00:21:30.790 --> 00:21:32.920
It was nothing. Anyway, I better be goin—

00:21:30.790 --> 00:21:31.850
Lemme see!

00:21:31.850 --> 00:21:32.920
I wanna see!

00:21:32.920 --> 00:21:33.440
Hey!

00:21:33.440 --> 00:21:35.550
Miss SDF member...

00:21:35.550 --> 00:21:36.310
What is it?

00:21:36.310 --> 00:21:39.280
What kind of job do you do here?

00:21:40.350 --> 00:21:41.940
I...

00:21:41.940 --> 00:21:44.110
I cook everyone's meals.

00:21:44.110 --> 00:21:45.410
I see...

00:21:45.410 --> 00:21:47.040
She's lying.

00:21:47.040 --> 00:21:49.490
Her rank insignia is that of a captain.

00:21:49.490 --> 00:21:52.580
She has the same rank as the captain of an Aegis Destroyer.

00:21:52.580 --> 00:21:56.630
Excuse me, but I have work to do, so I have to leave now.

00:21:56.630 --> 00:21:58.210
Thanks a lot!

00:21:58.210 --> 00:22:00.680
Oh, let me give you my business card!

00:22:01.670 --> 00:22:02.770
Sorry about this.

00:22:01.670 --> 00:22:05.810
Damn it! This jacket really gets in the way!

00:22:02.770 --> 00:22:05.810
Don't mind him, head back to work.

00:22:11.780 --> 00:22:13.790
What's with these flashy cards?

00:22:13.790 --> 00:22:14.890
Good catch, brat!

00:22:14.890 --> 00:22:16.100
Wait for me!

00:22:16.100 --> 00:22:17.650
You beautiful lady!

00:22:17.650 --> 00:22:20.320
What a disgrace...

00:22:20.320 --> 00:22:22.840
Sorry, Sonoko, could you hold these for a second?

00:22:22.840 --> 00:22:24.860
What's with these ugly cards?!

00:22:24.860 --> 00:22:29.950
He had them made recently, saying he wants to stand out at every crime scene.

00:22:29.950 --> 00:22:33.040
But I think he's missing the point a bit...

00:22:34.470 --> 00:22:37.400
Mitsuhiko, can I borrow your camera again?

00:22:37.400 --> 00:22:39.060
All right.

00:22:39.060 --> 00:22:39.810
Here.

00:22:39.810 --> 00:22:41.440
Give these cards to Ran-<i>neechan</i>.

00:22:41.440 --> 00:22:42.340
Okay.

00:22:42.340 --> 00:22:43.620
I've got to go to the toilet.

00:22:43.620 --> 00:22:44.160
Huh?!

00:22:44.160 --> 00:22:45.000
Conan-<i>kun</i>!

00:22:45.000 --> 00:22:47.260
What's he gonna take a photo of in the toilet?

00:22:48.810 --> 00:22:50.600
By the way, Ai-<i>kun</i>...

00:22:52.010 --> 00:22:53.060
What is it?

00:22:53.780 --> 00:22:57.630
I wonder if the kids liked the riddle I gave them earlier.

00:22:57.630 --> 00:23:00.190
They'd like it as long as the answer wasn't number four, his back, right?

00:23:03.770 --> 00:23:05.380
Hello.

00:23:05.380 --> 00:23:06.160
Doc...

00:23:06.160 --> 00:23:07.810
There's something I want you to investigate.

00:23:07.810 --> 00:23:09.240
Oh, it's you, Shin'ichi?

00:23:09.590 --> 00:23:10.730
Yeah...

00:23:10.730 --> 00:23:13.490
You sent a photo to Ai-<i>kun</i>'s phone?

00:23:15.320 --> 00:23:17.480
Got it, I'll check it out right away.

00:23:17.480 --> 00:23:20.750
By the way, did some kind of case happen?

00:23:20.750 --> 00:23:23.460
No, there's just something that I'm wondering about.

00:23:23.460 --> 00:23:24.580
Did she get the photo?

00:23:24.580 --> 00:23:27.090
Yeah, it was delivered fine.

00:23:27.320 --> 00:23:29.710
It looks like a female SDF member.

00:23:29.710 --> 00:23:31.320
Just the one photo, right?

00:23:31.320 --> 00:23:34.560
Yeah, I want you to look into what department the woman in the photo is stationed in.

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:42.760
Only 4% of the JMSDF's personnel are women, and many of them are used in adverts, so she shouldn't be hard to find.

00:23:42.760 --> 00:23:44.640
Okay, got it.

00:23:44.640 --> 00:23:47.060
Then we shouldn't have too much of a problem.

00:23:47.060 --> 00:23:49.990
By the way, about the quiz earlier...

00:23:50.570 --> 00:23:52.030
He hung up.

00:23:52.030 --> 00:23:53.700
What a shame, huh?

00:23:55.540 --> 00:23:57.340
A satellite transmission?

00:23:57.340 --> 00:23:59.160
Whereabouts on the deck?

00:23:59.160 --> 00:24:00.920
It's coming from the right side of the deck.

00:24:00.920 --> 00:24:03.640
That's near the civilians.

00:24:03.640 --> 00:24:04.760
Have it investigated.

00:24:04.760 --> 00:24:05.550
Yes, sir!

00:24:05.980 --> 00:24:07.880
This is a transmission from the CIC to all areas.

00:24:08.120 --> 00:24:13.100
A satellite transmission was detected on the right side of the deck. Watanabe and Abiko are to head there immediately...

00:24:08.120 --> 00:24:09.310
Captain!

00:24:09.860 --> 00:24:13.100
X couldn't be among the civilians, could he?

00:24:13.100 --> 00:24:17.480
Maybe the shipwreck earlier was connected with X as well...

00:24:18.680 --> 00:24:20.440
X...

00:24:20.440 --> 00:24:23.650
This radar could even be called the eyes of the Aegis.

00:24:23.650 --> 00:24:33.160
You wouldn't know just by looking at it, but this radar can cover over 450 km, and identify over 200 objects at once.

00:24:33.160 --> 00:24:34.390
Amazing!

00:24:34.390 --> 00:24:36.750
It really is a great detective of the seas!

00:24:36.750 --> 00:24:38.720
It's so cool!

00:24:39.450 --> 00:24:41.110
That place...?!

00:24:41.110 --> 00:24:43.580
That's where I just called the doc...

00:24:43.800 --> 00:24:46.600
Did they find out about my satellite communications?

00:24:46.600 --> 00:24:47.800
Or perhaps...

00:24:47.800 --> 00:24:53.760
The Aegis System is only given to countries trusted by the US, who developed it.

00:24:53.760 --> 00:25:00.230
And we, Japan, were the first country it was awarded to.

00:24:53.760 --> 00:24:55.550
Yeah, got it.

00:24:55.550 --> 00:24:58.120
I guess I better report it in.

00:24:58.120 --> 00:25:00.230
I'm counting on you. I'll check out the deck.

00:25:00.230 --> 00:25:06.210
Now, my next topic is the helicopter stationed at the stern: the SH-60K.

00:25:06.210 --> 00:25:08.680
Wow! They've even got a helicopter!

00:25:08.680 --> 00:25:10.950
Huh? What's wrong, Conan-<i>kun</i>?

00:25:09.340 --> 00:25:10.950
Whoa! How exciting!

00:25:10.950 --> 00:25:13.100
Oh, I gotta go to the toilet.

00:25:13.100 --> 00:25:14.610
Huh? Again?

00:25:14.610 --> 00:25:16.290
Hold on, Conan-<i>kun</i>!

00:25:16.290 --> 00:25:16.910
Huh?

00:25:16.910 --> 00:25:18.960
I'm going with you.

00:25:18.960 --> 00:25:20.440
Oh, you don't have to!

00:25:20.440 --> 00:25:21.420
Of course I do!

00:25:21.420 --> 00:25:23.750
You vanish as soon as I take my eyes off you!

00:25:23.750 --> 00:25:25.100
I don't—

00:25:25.100 --> 00:25:27.360
You just did, remember?

00:25:27.360 --> 00:25:28.130
Come on...

00:25:28.130 --> 00:25:29.500
Let's go together.

00:25:29.500 --> 00:25:30.800
Okay...

00:25:31.500 --> 00:25:35.220
I nearly got lost when I went to the toilet earlier too.

00:25:35.420 --> 00:25:37.690
This destroyer's full of twists and turns...

00:25:35.980 --> 00:25:38.800
Even though you're in high school?

00:25:39.590 --> 00:25:42.890
That's right, she's not too good with directions...

00:25:48.320 --> 00:25:51.490
Geez... How far away did you go?

00:25:51.490 --> 00:25:54.410
Sorry, sorry! I forgot the way back here.

00:25:54.410 --> 00:25:57.540
That's why I said I'd come with you.

00:25:57.540 --> 00:25:59.120
But...

00:25:59.120 --> 00:26:01.290
Don't go wandering off by yourself again, okay?

00:26:01.290 --> 00:26:04.170
Next time, you mightn't be able to find me.

00:26:04.170 --> 00:26:05.440
It's fine!

00:26:05.440 --> 00:26:06.250
Huh?

00:26:06.250 --> 00:26:08.350
No matter how lost I am,

00:26:08.350 --> 00:26:09.840
you'll always manage to find me, right?

00:26:10.920 --> 00:26:14.050
You're a great detective, after all!

00:26:17.760 --> 00:26:18.840
It's cold!

00:26:21.010 --> 00:26:22.280
Geez!

00:26:26.260 --> 00:26:27.440
Don't you worry!

00:26:27.440 --> 00:26:28.520
Huh?

00:26:29.780 --> 00:26:35.260
I'll always find you, wherever you are.

00:26:35.610 --> 00:26:37.260
That's for sure.

00:26:37.260 --> 00:26:38.330
Huh?

00:26:40.610 --> 00:26:43.040
I thought this way led to the toilet...

00:26:43.040 --> 00:26:43.540
Huh?

00:26:43.990 --> 00:26:46.490
Sorry, Conan-<i>kun</i>! Looks like I got us lost...

00:26:46.490 --> 00:26:49.640
Come on... Don't actually get us lost...

00:26:50.890 --> 00:26:53.070
What was that scream just now?

00:26:53.070 --> 00:26:54.170
Hey, Conan-<i>kun</i>!

00:26:54.330 --> 00:26:55.850
Sawamura-<i>san</i>!

00:26:55.850 --> 00:26:57.750
Something terrible got sucked in!

00:26:57.750 --> 00:26:59.220
Something terrible?

00:26:59.680 --> 00:27:01.740
Hey! Don't tell me that's a...?!

00:27:02.640 --> 00:27:03.520
You guys!

00:27:03.540 --> 00:27:04.600
Could it be?!

00:27:03.970 --> 00:27:05.770
This area's off-limits!

00:27:04.600 --> 00:27:06.430
That's a human arm!

00:27:05.770 --> 00:27:09.450
We're very sorry, we got lost on the way to the toilet...

00:27:06.810 --> 00:27:08.190
What a mess...

00:27:08.190 --> 00:27:09.140
What should we do?!

00:27:09.140 --> 00:27:12.970
For now, you better tell the Captain about this.

00:27:12.970 --> 00:27:13.650
Understood.

00:27:13.650 --> 00:27:17.230
I'll take these two children back to Chief Navigator Inoue.

00:27:13.650 --> 00:27:17.230
Ran-<i>neechan</i>, let's tell Uncle Kogorō.

00:27:17.230 --> 00:27:18.350
Roger.

00:27:17.230 --> 00:27:18.350
You're right.

00:27:18.350 --> 00:27:19.200
Umm...

00:27:19.200 --> 00:27:21.860
Maybe you should consult my father?

00:27:21.860 --> 00:27:22.380
Huh?

00:27:22.380 --> 00:27:25.730
It's a human arm that you have on that table, isn't it?

00:27:25.730 --> 00:27:26.660
That's...

00:27:27.060 --> 00:27:30.030
My father's Kogorō Mouri.

00:27:31.040 --> 00:27:33.090
Have you heard about him?

00:27:33.090 --> 00:27:35.950
He's the great detective known as ‘Sleeping Kogorō’.

00:27:35.960 --> 00:27:38.930
Kaihō
 School

00:27:40.320 --> 00:27:41.760
Yo! What's up, Kudō?

00:27:42.110 --> 00:27:44.190
Huh, a corpse?!

00:27:44.190 --> 00:27:46.350
Ya found a corpse aboard that Aegis Destroyer?

00:27:46.350 --> 00:27:49.810
No, all that was found was a left arm.

00:27:49.810 --> 00:27:50.810
But most likely...

00:27:55.150 --> 00:27:58.370
The left arm was clothed in a JMSDF uniform.

00:27:58.370 --> 00:28:00.660
So whoever was murdered was in the JMSDF?

00:28:00.660 --> 00:28:04.010
I don't know if it was a murder or an accident yet.

00:28:04.010 --> 00:28:06.660
But whoever died was a Lieutenant.

00:28:07.140 --> 00:28:08.700
Interestin'...

00:28:09.240 --> 00:28:10.790
'Kay, gotcha.

00:28:11.060 --> 00:28:12.170
I'll go there right now.

00:28:12.170 --> 00:28:13.490
I'll wait for your call.

00:28:13.490 --> 00:28:15.170
Found ya!

00:28:15.170 --> 00:28:17.570
Clubs have already started, you know?

00:28:17.570 --> 00:28:19.380
I ain't got time.

00:28:19.380 --> 00:28:20.450
Gotta go to Maizuru.

00:28:20.450 --> 00:28:21.050
Huh?

00:28:21.050 --> 00:28:22.450
Maizuru?

00:28:22.450 --> 00:28:24.260
Hey, Heiji!

00:28:28.200 --> 00:28:29.230
Nothing here.

00:28:29.230 --> 00:28:29.690
Yeah.

00:28:30.110 --> 00:28:32.810
We can't find any machine capable of satellite transmission.

00:28:33.240 --> 00:28:36.490
Keep checking the corners not covered by surveillance cameras.

00:28:33.240 --> 00:28:36.490
So they <i>did</i> find out about my transmissions...

00:28:36.490 --> 00:28:38.360
X may be hiding in a corner somewhere.

00:28:38.360 --> 00:28:38.820
Copy that.

00:28:38.820 --> 00:28:39.940
X?

00:28:39.940 --> 00:28:40.990
Oh, crap!

00:28:40.990 --> 00:28:43.280
What was that strange noise just now?

00:28:43.570 --> 00:28:46.490
Shin'ichi hung up on me...

00:28:46.910 --> 00:28:48.500
I wonder if something happened...

00:28:48.500 --> 00:28:51.960
And just when we were about to tell him what he asked us for...

00:29:05.410 --> 00:29:07.540
We must've just imagined it.

00:29:07.540 --> 00:29:07.890
Yeah.

00:29:08.280 --> 00:29:09.780
It was nothing.

00:29:09.780 --> 00:29:11.850
We'll keep looking.

00:29:11.850 --> 00:29:13.870
That was close!

00:29:13.870 --> 00:29:17.560
Well, this is an Aegis Destroyer. Top-notch security indeed.

00:29:19.120 --> 00:29:22.530
But I better find a different way to communicate...

00:29:22.830 --> 00:29:25.740
I'll be caught right away if I use that without permission.

00:29:28.350 --> 00:29:29.930
That mark...

00:29:29.930 --> 00:29:32.660
It's the mark signifying a strong magnetic field!

00:29:33.290 --> 00:29:35.000
This room should do...

00:29:35.000 --> 00:29:37.280
I'm the captain, Tateishi.

00:29:37.280 --> 00:29:38.700
You must be Mouri-<i>san</i>.

00:29:38.700 --> 00:29:41.720
The one and only Great Detective Kogorō Mouri, at your service.

00:29:42.030 --> 00:29:45.580
I heard about you from Capt. Sekiguchi.

00:29:44.220 --> 00:29:47.220
Wakasa Military Police

00:29:44.220 --> 00:29:47.220
Capt. Makoto Sekiguchi

00:29:45.580 --> 00:29:47.230
I'm Sekiguchi, from the Military Police.

00:29:47.230 --> 00:29:51.310
The Military Police are the
 internal police of the military, right?

00:29:51.310 --> 00:29:52.320
Correct.

00:29:52.320 --> 00:29:53.600
I see.

00:29:53.600 --> 00:29:57.040
So, this is the dismembered part of a corpse you mentioned?

00:29:57.040 --> 00:29:57.310
Yes.

00:29:57.710 --> 00:29:59.070
Here it is.

00:30:01.380 --> 00:30:02.540
I see...

00:30:02.540 --> 00:30:06.530
It doesn't seem to have been removed using a sharp blade.

00:30:06.530 --> 00:30:10.640
Also, the wound shows no signs of life.

00:30:10.640 --> 00:30:13.370
Then you're saying it was severed post-mortem?

00:30:13.370 --> 00:30:14.540
Correct.

00:30:14.540 --> 00:30:16.720
Where was this arm found?

00:30:16.720 --> 00:30:18.760
In the pumping system's filter.

00:30:19.820 --> 00:30:22.340
Wasn't the pumping system what we...?

00:30:22.340 --> 00:30:28.180
The sound you just heard was made by our pumping system letting in a large amount of sea water.

00:30:28.180 --> 00:30:30.680
So that's what happened when we heard that sound...!

00:30:30.680 --> 00:30:36.600
Sometimes, when leaving Maizuru Harbour, large pieces of debris carried by the ocean current are sucked up.

00:30:37.190 --> 00:30:40.650
This arm must've got stuck in the filter at that time.

00:30:40.650 --> 00:30:42.070
What do you mean by ‘the filter’?

00:30:42.070 --> 00:30:51.690
It's a net placed in the pump gate to stop large pieces of debris, fish, shells and so on from getting in when we draw in sea water.

00:30:53.000 --> 00:30:54.500
So how did <i>this</i> end up here?

00:30:54.500 --> 00:31:00.600
When a piece of debris obstructs the filter, we collect it to find out what it is.

00:31:00.600 --> 00:31:03.800
It's typically a large piece of seaweed or a plastic bag.

00:31:04.200 --> 00:31:06.630
By the way, do you have any idea who this arm belongs to?

00:31:09.090 --> 00:31:10.600
You do, don't you?

00:31:10.600 --> 00:31:13.060
Who is it, Capt. Tateishi?

00:31:14.520 --> 00:31:17.770
Judging from the rank markings
on the cuff and the wristwatch,

00:31:18.160 --> 00:31:21.110
I think it's Lt. Sasaura from the Wakasa base.

00:31:22.020 --> 00:31:27.110
When I asked the base to check, they told me they didn't know the whereabouts of Lt. Sasaura.

00:31:27.130 --> 00:31:29.530
Then you're probably right.

00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:32.640
His watch stopped at 5:30 AM.

00:31:32.640 --> 00:31:34.870
How can you tell that it's AM?

00:31:34.870 --> 00:31:37.580
Look at the position of the calendar.

00:31:37.580 --> 00:31:39.950
You can still see a part of yesterday's date,

00:31:39.950 --> 00:31:42.460
so it had to have been in the morning.

00:31:42.800 --> 00:31:46.300
Sasaura-<i>san</i> was one of the people who normally boards this Aegis Destroyer, right?

00:31:46.660 --> 00:31:50.260
He sometimes comes aboard, but he wasn't planned to be in today's shift.

00:31:50.720 --> 00:31:54.800
You started the pumping system when we left Maizuru Harbour, right?

00:31:54.800 --> 00:31:55.810
Yes.

00:31:55.810 --> 00:32:00.400
I think this left arm got severed by the pump gate at that time.

00:32:00.400 --> 00:32:01.400
I see.

00:32:01.860 --> 00:32:09.000
So at the time, his body was already drifting in the sea, near Maizuru Harbour.

00:32:09.000 --> 00:32:13.850
Then, the pumping system activated, and his body was sucked in with the sea water.

00:32:13.850 --> 00:32:18.790
But his body got caught at the entrance, and only his left arm made it as far as the filter.

00:32:18.790 --> 00:32:20.740
Am I right?

00:32:20.740 --> 00:32:21.730
Yes.

00:32:21.730 --> 00:32:23.300
I believe you're correct.

00:32:23.300 --> 00:32:26.170
And when do we get back to the harbour?

00:32:26.170 --> 00:32:28.130
We plan to return at 5:30 PM.

00:32:28.370 --> 00:32:33.980
Then you should contact the Kyōto Police so they can be ready to conduct an autopsy as soon as we get back.

00:32:28.890 --> 00:32:34.460
This doesn't look good. Looking at his arm, it needs to be taken for an autopsy soon.

00:32:33.980 --> 00:32:37.450
Understood. I'll call them right away.

00:32:35.580 --> 00:32:37.350
Oh, yeah!

00:32:37.350 --> 00:32:39.270
There's a helicopter on this ship!

00:32:40.100 --> 00:32:41.790
Wow, amazing!

00:32:41.790 --> 00:32:43.360
This is where you drive the ship!

00:32:43.360 --> 00:32:44.700
Conan-<i>kun</i>...

00:32:44.700 --> 00:32:47.230
Hey, brat, don't stick your nose where it doesn't belong!

00:32:47.230 --> 00:32:51.350
I heard your voice while looking for the helicopter, Uncle!

00:32:51.350 --> 00:32:52.450
Helicopter?

00:32:52.870 --> 00:32:53.920
I see...

00:32:53.920 --> 00:32:55.160
We can take the arm to shore immediately with the helicopter.

00:32:55.160 --> 00:32:58.580
But the passengers might notice if we send out the helicopter.

00:32:58.580 --> 00:33:00.650
This isn't the time to be worrying about that!

00:33:00.650 --> 00:33:01.480
Mouri-<i>san</i>...

00:33:02.000 --> 00:33:06.900
If the civilians find out about this, it may cause a panic.

00:33:06.900 --> 00:33:09.590
I wish I could see the helicopter flying!

00:33:10.040 --> 00:33:12.430
Like when you showed us the cannon before!

00:33:13.350 --> 00:33:16.820
If you pretend you're doing a demonstration like you did earlier and make the helicopter fly...

00:33:16.820 --> 00:33:17.770
You're right!

00:33:17.770 --> 00:33:20.720
We can avoid exposure that way!

00:33:20.720 --> 00:33:21.910
Capt. Tateishi.

00:33:22.690 --> 00:33:24.480
There's no time to waste.

00:33:26.070 --> 00:33:27.110
Understood.

00:33:27.110 --> 00:33:29.150
I'll get the helicopter ready straight away.

00:33:29.150 --> 00:33:31.860
Tōkyō Police HQ

00:33:29.980 --> 00:33:30.650
What?

00:33:30.650 --> 00:33:31.860
On an Aegis Destroyer?

00:33:32.990 --> 00:33:34.280
Got it.

00:33:34.280 --> 00:33:36.450
We'll contact the Kyōto Police right away.

00:33:37.050 --> 00:33:40.290
And we'll head there too as soon as we get authorisation to come aboard.

00:33:40.290 --> 00:33:42.540
Please do.

00:33:42.540 --> 00:33:45.750
There's a chance that the killer's
 still aboard this Aegis Destroyer.

00:33:46.860 --> 00:33:51.470
First of all, I'm counting on you to investigate this left arm.

00:33:59.130 --> 00:34:03.230
And now we'll show a demonstration
 of the helicopter taking off.

00:34:04.600 --> 00:34:08.110
It would be dangerous to get any closer, so please stay behind the barrier.

00:34:09.040 --> 00:34:10.050
Phew.

00:34:10.050 --> 00:34:11.300
Somehow, we made it in time.

00:34:12.870 --> 00:34:13.750
You're...

00:34:14.530 --> 00:34:15.590
What's wrong?

00:34:15.590 --> 00:34:17.200
Did you lose your dad again?

00:34:17.950 --> 00:34:19.770
You were alone before too.

00:34:21.070 --> 00:34:23.000
Are you okay?

00:34:23.430 --> 00:34:25.050
Where are your parents?

00:34:26.460 --> 00:34:30.120
His father's supposed to be here, but it seems he got lost.

00:34:30.120 --> 00:34:31.050
Really?

00:34:32.120 --> 00:34:34.670
Your name was Yūki-<i>kun</i>, right?

00:34:35.500 --> 00:34:36.180
Yeah.

00:34:36.690 --> 00:34:39.250
Then you stay with him, Conan-<i>kun</i>.

00:34:39.250 --> 00:34:42.060
I'll talk to an SDF member about Yūki-<i>kun</i>'s situation.

00:34:42.400 --> 00:34:44.520
Stop! If you do that...

00:34:45.220 --> 00:34:46.400
If I do that...?

00:34:47.560 --> 00:34:49.860
I'm fine.

00:34:50.740 --> 00:34:51.690
I'm fine!

00:34:51.690 --> 00:34:53.400
Hold on, Yūki-<i>kun</i>!

00:34:58.000 --> 00:34:59.410
Here, you dropped these.

00:35:00.410 --> 00:35:01.450
What kind of medicine is it?

00:35:02.090 --> 00:35:03.580
It's for hives.

00:35:03.580 --> 00:35:05.100
It stops me itching.

00:35:05.100 --> 00:35:06.040
Do you have problems often?

00:35:06.770 --> 00:35:09.100
I can't drink things with milk.

00:35:09.100 --> 00:35:11.480
Oh, food allergies.

00:35:12.380 --> 00:35:13.700
Wait, Yūki-<i>kun</i>!

00:35:15.130 --> 00:35:16.470
Dad told me...

00:35:17.560 --> 00:35:18.930
‘You'll be strong!

00:35:19.420 --> 00:35:21.800
That's why I named you “Yūki”.’

00:35:19.420 --> 00:35:21.800
courage

00:35:22.760 --> 00:35:24.670
So I'm fine!

00:35:24.670 --> 00:35:26.020
Yūki!

00:35:26.580 --> 00:35:28.210
So that's where you were!

00:35:28.910 --> 00:35:30.420
Are you his father?

00:35:30.420 --> 00:35:31.250
Yes.

00:35:31.250 --> 00:35:33.980
Great. It seems he got lost...

00:35:34.420 --> 00:35:36.310
Sorry for the bother.

00:35:36.990 --> 00:35:39.990
See, that's what happens when you wander off on your own.

00:36:00.770 --> 00:36:03.640
Hey, aren't we in Maizuru now?

00:36:04.100 --> 00:36:04.950
Yeah.

00:36:04.950 --> 00:36:07.410
But first, we gotta get some intel nearby.

00:36:08.950 --> 00:36:10.480
What's with all those people?

00:36:11.740 --> 00:36:14.570
To think something like that
 happened on that Aegis Destroyer...

00:36:15.010 --> 00:36:16.810
I was surprised too, to be honest.

00:36:16.810 --> 00:36:19.030
There's a lot of noise. What's going on?

00:36:19.030 --> 00:36:22.490
Oh, I'm in hiding so my satellite
 transmissions don't get traced.

00:36:22.950 --> 00:36:25.410
That way you're protected against being traced.

00:36:25.760 --> 00:36:27.770
So, what about that SDF lady?

00:36:27.770 --> 00:36:30.480
I searched, but I couldn't find any
 SDF member that looks like her.

00:36:33.340 --> 00:36:35.080
It really is a person!

00:36:35.080 --> 00:36:36.520
Heiji, what is it?

00:36:36.520 --> 00:36:38.570
Don't worry, just wait for me here.

00:36:38.570 --> 00:36:39.800
Wait, Heiji!

00:36:40.740 --> 00:36:42.010
He doesn't have any left arm!

00:36:42.990 --> 00:36:44.160
Did you call the police?

00:36:44.160 --> 00:36:45.350
They're coming now.

00:36:45.350 --> 00:36:47.850
A corpse without a left arm?

00:36:48.890 --> 00:36:50.560
A lieutenant's stripes.

00:36:51.110 --> 00:36:52.400
There's no doubt then.

00:36:52.400 --> 00:36:54.900
It's the body of Sasaura-<i>san</i> — the guy Kudō was talkin' about.

00:36:56.000 --> 00:36:57.030
Is that blood?

00:36:58.330 --> 00:36:59.620
No, it ain't blood.

00:36:59.620 --> 00:37:00.840
Then what is it?

00:37:01.750 --> 00:37:03.470
You can't, you can't!

00:37:03.470 --> 00:37:04.840
What is it, kid?

00:37:04.840 --> 00:37:08.700
You can't touch or move the body until the police arrive!

00:37:22.570 --> 00:37:24.720
I'm Megure from the Tōkyō Police.

00:37:24.720 --> 00:37:27.850
We came on board along with these people from the Wakasa Coast Guard.

00:37:28.450 --> 00:37:31.230
Welcome. I'm Tateishi, the Captain.

00:37:31.920 --> 00:37:32.800
I'm Satō.

00:37:32.800 --> 00:37:34.020
I'm Takagi.

00:37:34.020 --> 00:37:37.360
Wakasa Coast Guard Security Dept.

00:37:34.020 --> 00:37:37.360
Masaaki Kurata

00:37:34.180 --> 00:37:36.100
I'm Kurata from the Security Department.

00:37:35.770 --> 00:37:37.360
Tsutomu Munekawa

00:37:35.770 --> 00:37:37.360
Wakasa Coast Guard Criminal Affairs

00:37:36.100 --> 00:37:37.360
I'm Munekawa from Criminal Affairs.

00:37:37.880 --> 00:37:39.580
Let's talk inside.

00:37:39.580 --> 00:37:40.350
Right.

00:37:42.350 --> 00:37:43.090
 What?

00:37:43.090 --> 00:37:44.530
At the shipyard in Wakasa Bay?

00:37:45.000 --> 00:37:45.800
Yeah.

00:37:45.800 --> 00:37:46.900
I'm pretty sure.

00:37:46.900 --> 00:37:49.490
The body has the same rank and missin' body part.

00:37:49.920 --> 00:37:56.960
That means Sasaura-<i>san</i> got his arm swallowed by the Aegis Destroyer at Maizuru Harbour, and then his corpse drifted here.

00:37:56.960 --> 00:37:59.510
It drifted...? But how?

00:37:59.510 --> 00:38:03.010
Wouldn't it have drifted on the ocean currents?

00:38:03.010 --> 00:38:04.550
Is there even a current going that way?

00:38:04.930 --> 00:38:06.550
Well, I'll check into that.

00:38:06.550 --> 00:38:10.060
Along with the substance I found on his body.

00:38:10.640 --> 00:38:11.980
Substance?

00:38:11.980 --> 00:38:15.770
Yeah. I don't know what it is, but there was a red substance on his neck.

00:38:16.350 --> 00:38:17.950
A red substance...

00:38:19.240 --> 00:38:21.740
Hattori, meet up with Dr. Agasa.

00:38:25.350 --> 00:38:27.200
Chow time!

00:38:28.480 --> 00:38:29.370
Yummy!

00:38:29.780 --> 00:38:32.280
Navy curry is so good!

00:38:32.280 --> 00:38:34.830
It's the best curry I've ever had!

00:38:38.140 --> 00:38:40.140
Right, it's really good!

00:38:41.980 --> 00:38:42.840
Yūki-<i>kun</i>...

00:38:47.650 --> 00:38:49.500
Maybe I'm just overthinking this.

00:38:49.500 --> 00:38:52.200
I wish I could cook curry like this!

00:38:53.200 --> 00:38:55.520
‘Yes, yes, it's really nice!’

00:38:55.520 --> 00:38:56.390
What?

00:38:56.390 --> 00:39:02.560
Why don't you call him saying ‘I cooked you some delicious curry, so hurry back!’

00:39:02.560 --> 00:39:05.700
Don't be stupid. He won't come back just for curry.

00:39:07.030 --> 00:39:08.010
She's right.

00:39:09.400 --> 00:39:11.080
I'll go call him.

00:39:11.080 --> 00:39:12.050
Now you've got it!

00:39:12.050 --> 00:39:13.750
No, it's not that.

00:39:13.750 --> 00:39:16.020
I just have something I want to tell Shin'ichi.

00:39:16.020 --> 00:39:18.210
Yeah, yeah. See ya!

00:39:18.210 --> 00:39:21.050
What does she want to tell me?

00:39:21.050 --> 00:39:22.250
Oh no, she's gonna call me!

00:39:23.300 --> 00:39:24.640
Conan-<i>kun</i>, where are you going?

00:39:24.640 --> 00:39:25.750
To the toilet.

00:39:25.750 --> 00:39:27.240
Again?

00:39:27.240 --> 00:39:28.590
I'll be back soon!

00:39:29.600 --> 00:39:33.220
That's my deduction and everything we know so far.

00:39:33.550 --> 00:39:34.550
I see.

00:39:34.550 --> 00:39:39.200
So there hasn't been a thorough investigation yet due to the public exercises.

00:39:39.200 --> 00:39:39.690
Right.

00:39:39.690 --> 00:39:41.800
Where are the civilians now?

00:39:41.800 --> 00:39:44.550
Eating lunch in the cafeteria.

00:39:44.550 --> 00:39:48.530
Then now would be the perfect time to investigate the areas open to the public.

00:39:48.530 --> 00:39:54.200
But I heard that Lt. Sasaura's body was found at a shipyard in Wakasa Bay.

00:39:54.200 --> 00:39:56.200
Do we need a thorough investigation?

00:39:56.200 --> 00:39:57.730
Just to make sure.

00:39:57.730 --> 00:40:01.850
There's still the possibility that he got sucked into the pump gate <i>before</i> the ship departed.

00:40:03.940 --> 00:40:05.400
Understood.

00:40:05.400 --> 00:40:07.090
I'll guide you around.

00:40:10.980 --> 00:40:11.430
That you, Ran?

00:40:12.480 --> 00:40:14.140
How did you know it's me?

00:40:14.720 --> 00:40:16.970
Never mind that, just tell me what's up.

00:40:16.970 --> 00:40:17.980
Never mind? But...

00:40:19.130 --> 00:40:20.960
Well, Shin'ichi, at the moment...

00:40:20.960 --> 00:40:22.310
...you're aboard an Aegis Destroyer, right?

00:40:23.210 --> 00:40:25.980
You're really lucky. I'd love to ride on one too!

00:40:25.980 --> 00:40:28.150
Wait, how did you know?

00:40:28.150 --> 00:40:29.670
Didn't I tell you before?

00:40:29.670 --> 00:40:32.410
I can find you no matter where you are.

00:40:33.560 --> 00:40:34.950
Shin'ichi...

00:40:35.590 --> 00:40:36.950
Oh, I get it!

00:40:36.950 --> 00:40:38.160
It was Conan-<i>kun</i>!

00:40:38.160 --> 00:40:40.190
He told you over the phone!

00:40:40.190 --> 00:40:41.620
Y-Yeah.

00:40:42.350 --> 00:40:44.290
Don't worry.

00:40:44.290 --> 00:40:45.950
I'll finish up the case soon.

00:40:47.290 --> 00:40:49.960
Don't say things you don't mean when you're that far away.

00:40:50.600 --> 00:40:51.720
What about it?

00:40:52.040 --> 00:40:54.220
You don't feel safe if I'm not with you or something?

00:40:55.070 --> 00:40:56.600
What are you talking about?

00:40:57.000 --> 00:40:58.600
That makes no sense!

00:40:58.600 --> 00:41:00.500
That's the spirit!

00:41:00.500 --> 00:41:01.020
See ya!

00:41:01.020 --> 00:41:02.310
Do your best!

00:41:02.900 --> 00:41:04.300
Wait!

00:41:07.930 --> 00:41:09.620
Though I'm actually pretty close to you.

00:41:14.800 --> 00:41:16.330
Jerk.

00:41:18.470 --> 00:41:21.800
It seems Inspector Megure's group found it on the deck.

00:41:21.800 --> 00:41:23.130
Where on the deck?

00:41:23.130 --> 00:41:24.440
I don't know that...

00:41:24.440 --> 00:41:26.290
Anyway, let's hurry.

00:41:26.850 --> 00:41:28.810
Did they find something on the deck?

00:41:30.040 --> 00:41:31.310
Over here!

00:41:31.310 --> 00:41:32.900
Yes, right here.

00:41:32.900 --> 00:41:37.880
Sasaura-<i>san</i>'s mobile phone was on these missile launchers.

00:41:37.880 --> 00:41:39.060
Where exactly?

00:41:39.420 --> 00:41:40.810
In this gap.

00:41:41.450 --> 00:41:42.230
Let me see.

00:41:42.700 --> 00:41:44.460
When was it last used?

00:41:44.460 --> 00:41:46.560
The last e-mail was yesterday after 9 PM.

00:41:46.950 --> 00:41:50.300
And the last call was this morning at 5:30.

00:41:50.300 --> 00:41:51.650
5:30 this morning?

00:41:51.650 --> 00:41:54.240
That's when his wristwatch stopped.

00:41:54.240 --> 00:41:56.550
It's also his estimated time of death.

00:41:57.500 --> 00:42:02.460
According to the autopsy, Sasaura-<i>san</i> died this morning between 4 and 6.

00:42:02.770 --> 00:42:06.790
In other words, Sasaura-<i>san</i> was aboard this Aegis Destroyer until then.

00:42:06.790 --> 00:42:09.000
Did you find out the cause of death?

00:42:09.000 --> 00:42:09.950
Yes.

00:42:09.950 --> 00:42:10.920
Drowning.

00:42:10.920 --> 00:42:15.840
So are you saying Sasaura-<i>san</i> fell from this Aegis Destroyer at 5:30 AM?

00:42:16.220 --> 00:42:17.600
It seems so.

00:42:17.600 --> 00:42:19.430
I see, I got it!

00:42:19.720 --> 00:42:24.020
At 5:30 this morning, Sasaura-<i>san</i> was fighting with someone right here.

00:42:24.330 --> 00:42:26.270
That's when he dropped his phone.

00:42:26.810 --> 00:42:30.530
Then, Sasaura-<i>san</i> ran away, but was probably trapped somewhere nearby.

00:42:30.530 --> 00:42:32.740
And then he was pushed into the sea.

00:42:33.140 --> 00:42:35.570
If you're right, it's a homicide.

00:42:35.570 --> 00:42:42.440
Then Sasaura-<i>san</i>'s body was swallowed by the ship's pump gate and got stuck in there before the departure.

00:42:42.440 --> 00:42:43.410
Yes.

00:42:43.800 --> 00:42:52.790
Then the ship's pumping system was started again after they left Maizuru Harbour, severing Sasaura-<i>san</i>'s arm.

00:42:53.430 --> 00:43:00.140
Then, his body drifting in the sea was taken to Wakasa Bay by the ocean current.

00:43:00.650 --> 00:43:04.570
Thinking about it, the fact that his phone is here also—

00:43:05.780 --> 00:43:08.730
This phone has the microSD card slot open!

00:43:08.730 --> 00:43:10.980
I don't remember it being open earlier.

00:43:11.400 --> 00:43:12.800
Does it have a card in there?

00:43:12.800 --> 00:43:14.050
No.

00:43:14.050 --> 00:43:15.740
Could the killer have taken it?

00:43:15.740 --> 00:43:20.700
So the killer murdered Sasaura-<i>san</i> in order to steal the data card from his phone!

00:43:20.700 --> 00:43:24.120
Damn, I can't see the phone from here...

00:43:24.740 --> 00:43:26.550
I guess I'll have to get closer.

00:43:32.930 --> 00:43:33.770
I won't let you get away!

00:43:36.430 --> 00:43:38.050
What is it, Mouri-<i>kun</i>?

00:43:38.050 --> 00:43:39.480
No, it's nothing...

00:43:43.520 --> 00:43:44.560
Upstairs?

00:43:52.290 --> 00:43:52.860
No...

00:43:53.450 --> 00:43:54.320
It's broken!

00:43:57.230 --> 00:43:58.030
What happened?

00:44:05.270 --> 00:44:05.700
What?

00:44:05.700 --> 00:44:07.130
The captain's quarters?

00:44:30.310 --> 00:44:31.770
That's a microSD card!

00:44:32.860 --> 00:44:33.310
Go!

00:44:37.190 --> 00:44:39.860
So this really is the data...

00:44:39.860 --> 00:44:41.700
I'll be in my room.

00:44:41.700 --> 00:44:44.550
Call me as soon as you find out something.

00:44:44.550 --> 00:44:46.110
Oh, Captain!

00:44:46.110 --> 00:44:47.640
Can I take a photo with you?

00:44:48.330 --> 00:44:52.670
Kid, this area is off-limits, so how about we take the photo over there?

00:44:52.670 --> 00:44:54.010
Okay!

00:45:05.150 --> 00:45:07.860
Figures — she removed the data card.

00:45:08.500 --> 00:45:12.470
But she didn't have time to completely delete the data she extracted on this computer.

00:45:15.990 --> 00:45:17.690
So where is the phone now?

00:45:18.330 --> 00:45:19.760
In the meeting room.

00:45:19.760 --> 00:45:21.650
And the Tōkyō Police?

00:45:21.650 --> 00:45:23.510
They're inspecting the contents of the phone.

00:45:22.230 --> 00:45:23.910
Why is the Captain here?

00:45:24.300 --> 00:45:25.800
Oh, crap.

00:45:25.800 --> 00:45:26.410
That voice was...

00:45:39.450 --> 00:45:40.590
Did she figure it out?

00:45:41.550 --> 00:45:42.860
If only I had more time...!

00:45:49.890 --> 00:45:50.970
Don't move!

00:45:52.020 --> 00:45:52.760
He got me!

00:45:56.700 --> 00:45:59.280
Damn, I didn't manage to copy everything.

00:45:59.280 --> 00:46:01.320
Why would X be interested in this data now...?

00:46:01.820 --> 00:46:02.610
X?

00:46:01.820 --> 00:46:03.920
I better put everything back the way it was.

00:46:03.920 --> 00:46:04.820
That reminds me...

00:46:05.070 --> 00:46:07.230
We couldn't find any traces of X either.

00:46:07.230 --> 00:46:08.620
X?

00:46:09.250 --> 00:46:13.670
Anyway, I better get out of here as soon as possible, and send what I could copy to the doc.

00:46:14.430 --> 00:46:15.830
No, wait.

00:46:16.410 --> 00:46:21.170
If I make a satellite transmission
 here, I might find out who she is.

00:46:24.330 --> 00:46:25.760
I'm getting satellite signals again!

00:46:26.730 --> 00:46:28.360
They're coming from the captain's quarters!

00:46:28.360 --> 00:46:29.320
What?

00:46:29.320 --> 00:46:30.810
The Captain's in a meeting now.

00:46:31.250 --> 00:46:33.710
Could it be X?

00:46:33.710 --> 00:46:36.260
Go confirm the Captain's whereabouts!

00:46:36.260 --> 00:46:36.810
Sir.

00:46:38.620 --> 00:46:39.950
This is a problem.

00:46:39.950 --> 00:46:42.570
There's important data in the captain's quarters.

00:46:44.820 --> 00:46:47.050
Download complete.

00:46:47.050 --> 00:46:50.660
What did Shin'ichi send us this time?

00:46:51.080 --> 00:46:52.100
Who knows?

00:46:52.100 --> 00:46:56.120
But since it's from Kudō-<i>kun</i>,
 I suppose he wants us to investigate it.

00:46:56.120 --> 00:46:58.420
Oh, we've arrived in Kyōto!

00:47:00.290 --> 00:47:01.420
Don't move!

00:47:03.940 --> 00:47:05.090
What are you doing here?

00:47:06.230 --> 00:47:08.300
You don't need to know.

00:47:08.300 --> 00:47:09.220
Capt. Fujii.

00:47:10.090 --> 00:47:11.500
Was it you?

00:47:11.500 --> 00:47:13.770
Captain, I'll explain later.

00:47:14.850 --> 00:47:16.560
Oh, it's you!

00:47:17.600 --> 00:47:18.230
Who is she?

00:47:18.560 --> 00:47:20.050
It's okay.

00:47:20.890 --> 00:47:22.350
Please get out.

00:47:22.350 --> 00:47:22.980
Yes.

00:47:24.200 --> 00:47:25.730
Wait!

00:47:25.730 --> 00:47:29.030
We came here because a
 suspicious transmission was detected!

00:47:29.350 --> 00:47:32.170
Yes, and when we arrived, she was here.

00:47:32.170 --> 00:47:35.250
I think we have the right to ask your identity.

00:47:35.610 --> 00:47:40.790
I'm sorry, but we can't reveal her identity to outsiders.

00:47:40.790 --> 00:47:42.600
Outsiders?

00:47:42.600 --> 00:47:43.940
Are you joking?

00:47:43.940 --> 00:47:44.850
They're right!

00:47:44.850 --> 00:47:49.340
Be it the police or the Coast Guard, we're all partners investigating this case, aren't we?

00:47:50.950 --> 00:47:55.010
Ah! It's the SDF lady!

00:47:55.010 --> 00:47:56.430
You're wandering around again?!

00:47:56.430 --> 00:48:01.810
A friend told me it's very rare for an SDF lady to be aboard an Aegis Destroyer.

00:48:02.020 --> 00:48:03.770
That's enough from you...

00:48:03.770 --> 00:48:04.900
He's right!

00:48:04.900 --> 00:48:07.990
Are female SDF officers even allowed to be on board an Aegis Destroyer?

00:48:08.880 --> 00:48:09.950
Yes.

00:48:09.950 --> 00:48:14.700
There are recent plans that allow female SDF officers aboard Aegis Destroyers too.

00:48:14.700 --> 00:48:17.450
So she's here to guide civilians around...

00:48:17.450 --> 00:48:19.920
I see. That explains it.

00:48:19.920 --> 00:48:24.170
Huh? But she said earlier that she was in charge of cooking!

00:48:25.060 --> 00:48:27.370
Ah, that's right.

00:48:27.370 --> 00:48:28.800
How do you explain that?

00:48:29.400 --> 00:48:31.490
Well...

00:48:31.490 --> 00:48:38.710
If you keep acting like this, we'll have no choice but to assume Sasaura-<i>san</i>'s killer is one of you.

00:48:38.710 --> 00:48:39.560
Wait.

00:48:40.030 --> 00:48:43.260
We'll cooperate as much as we can.

00:48:43.260 --> 00:48:43.950
Captain!

00:48:45.030 --> 00:48:48.720
Since things turned out this way, 
maybe we should tell them...

00:48:48.720 --> 00:48:49.400
Yes.

00:48:51.500 --> 00:48:54.990
I'm a member of Intelligence Security Command.

00:48:55.420 --> 00:48:57.080
Intelligence Security Command?

00:48:57.080 --> 00:48:59.210
The one that reports directly to the Minister of Defence?

00:48:59.690 --> 00:49:00.730
Yes.

00:49:00.730 --> 00:49:05.670
Our job is to manage the SDF's information and to monitor the ideologies of SDF members.{thoughtpolice?!}


00:49:05.670 --> 00:49:10.320
But why is a Intelligence Security Command member on this Aegis Destroyer?

00:49:10.320 --> 00:49:13.140
Oh! It's because of the suspicious boat found this morning, isn't it?

00:49:13.140 --> 00:49:14.260
Yes.

00:49:14.260 --> 00:49:17.640
We think it might be a spy ship from a certain country.

00:49:18.170 --> 00:49:25.400
There <i>was</i> an antenna for wireless communication, as well as a bomb planted to blow it up.

00:49:27.150 --> 00:49:29.120
You sure know a lot about it.

00:49:29.120 --> 00:49:31.850
I was the one who found that suspicious boat.

00:49:33.080 --> 00:49:35.160
That's why I was put on this investigation.

00:49:35.160 --> 00:49:40.520
Since the suspicious boat was found near Maizuru Harbour, where this Aegis Destroyer was anchored,

00:49:40.520 --> 00:49:44.510
we believe a spy might be on board.

00:49:44.510 --> 00:49:45.500
A spy?

00:49:45.500 --> 00:49:49.380
Yes. In our investigations, we named him ‘X’.

00:49:49.740 --> 00:49:50.910
X?

00:49:50.910 --> 00:49:53.050
What's the spy's goal?

00:49:53.050 --> 00:49:57.510
We believe he is trying to obtain classified intel on Aegis Destroyers.

00:49:57.510 --> 00:49:59.810
Intel?

00:49:59.810 --> 00:50:02.350
What would happen if that intel leaked out?

00:50:02.920 --> 00:50:08.640
We'd lose a lot of trust with the US, who provided the Aegis system.

00:50:08.640 --> 00:50:14.650
But more importantly, if the routes of the Aegis Destroyers leak out,

00:50:14.650 --> 00:50:18.200
then Japan's line of defence would be known by everybody.

00:50:18.200 --> 00:50:22.830
We'd be defenceless to military
 aggression from other countries.

00:50:22.830 --> 00:50:28.040
In other words, it would cause a national crisis.

00:50:31.500 --> 00:50:36.850
Can I presume then that the victim, Sasaura-<i>san</i>, knew about the spy?

00:50:36.850 --> 00:50:37.260
Yes.

00:50:37.730 --> 00:50:40.050
He knew about it because of his job.

00:50:40.050 --> 00:50:41.280
His job?

00:50:42.340 --> 00:50:44.630
What was Sasaura-<i>san</i>'s job?

00:50:45.260 --> 00:50:47.810
As a Lieutenant, he was part of management, right?

00:50:49.250 --> 00:50:54.200
Lt. Sasaura was the Director of Intelligence for the Wakasa JMSDF base.

00:50:54.200 --> 00:50:55.850
Director of Intelligence?

00:50:55.850 --> 00:50:58.410
His duty was to safeguard information on Aegis Destroyers.

00:50:59.650 --> 00:51:03.550
And so he was murdered by X, who wanted to steal that information!

00:51:03.550 --> 00:51:08.000
So whoever took the data card from Sasaura-<i>san</i>'s phone is X?

00:51:08.000 --> 00:51:10.680
No doubt about that.

00:51:08.840 --> 00:51:11.500
No, <i>she</i> took the card out...

00:51:10.680 --> 00:51:13.180
Then we should search this ship for X.

00:51:11.950 --> 00:51:14.840
But why is she keeping silent about it?

00:51:14.840 --> 00:51:17.060
Excuse me, please let us through.

00:51:17.740 --> 00:51:21.430
Sorry, but we have to inspect the communication tools in this room.

00:51:21.760 --> 00:51:24.550
We will also have to inspect your belongings, so don't leave the room.

00:51:22.300 --> 00:51:23.200
Crap!

00:51:24.950 --> 00:51:26.270
Hey, Uncle!

00:51:27.230 --> 00:51:28.580
What?

00:51:28.580 --> 00:51:31.790
I forgot I ordered an extra portion of curry.

00:51:31.790 --> 00:51:32.940
Curry?

00:51:32.940 --> 00:51:36.280
Geez, what are you doing here in the first place?!

00:51:36.280 --> 00:51:37.720
Hurry up and get out!

00:51:37.720 --> 00:51:38.610
Okay!

00:51:39.410 --> 00:51:40.450
Nice, old man!

00:51:53.100 --> 00:51:54.460
Welcome.

00:51:59.930 --> 00:52:01.270
Hattori, can you hear me?

00:52:01.990 --> 00:52:05.190
Yeah, I met up with Dr. Agasa.

00:52:05.190 --> 00:52:07.100
Did you find out anything about the red substance?

00:52:07.570 --> 00:52:09.130
We're examinin' it now.

00:52:09.130 --> 00:52:10.830
Hold on.

00:52:10.830 --> 00:52:14.780
Though, bein' able to do an examination like this in a car is pretty awesome!

00:52:15.200 --> 00:52:17.800
Well, Ai-<i>kun</i> was a scientist, after all.

00:52:17.800 --> 00:52:18.890
A scientist?

00:52:18.890 --> 00:52:22.150
What are you blabberin' about? She's just a little kid.

00:52:22.150 --> 00:52:24.740
Don't mind her age.

00:52:26.180 --> 00:52:27.500
Got it. This is it.

00:52:29.080 --> 00:52:30.420
TBT?

00:52:30.780 --> 00:52:32.190
Anti-fouling paint.

00:52:32.800 --> 00:52:34.000
A special paint used for ships.

00:52:34.490 --> 00:52:35.960
Ship paint?

00:52:35.960 --> 00:52:40.050
Can you check if that paint is from this Aegis Destroyer?

00:52:40.050 --> 00:52:42.680
Got it. I'll get the little lady to check it now.

00:52:42.680 --> 00:52:44.620
The little lady?

00:52:44.620 --> 00:52:47.140
Oh, and about the ocean currents...

00:52:47.140 --> 00:52:52.480
There wasn't any current that could've brought Sasaura-<i>san</i>'s body from Maizuru Harbour to Wakasa Bay.

00:52:53.480 --> 00:52:56.620
So how'd the body end up in Wakasa Bay?

00:52:56.620 --> 00:52:58.690
Oh, and what about the data I sent you?

00:52:58.690 --> 00:52:59.830
Oh, that?

00:53:00.670 --> 00:53:03.200
Kudō wants to ask you somethin' about the data you got earlier.

00:53:04.650 --> 00:53:08.910
Shin'ichi, it looks like it's a piece of data about the Aegis Destroyers.

00:53:08.910 --> 00:53:10.190
I knew it.

00:53:10.900 --> 00:53:14.670
And there are some traces showing it was copied from a certain company's cloud.

00:53:14.670 --> 00:53:18.650
By cloud, you mean a service to store data on the Internet?

00:53:18.650 --> 00:53:25.350
Yes. If we can work out the ID and password, we should be able to get the original data from the cloud.

00:53:26.900 --> 00:53:28.290
I see...

00:53:28.290 --> 00:53:33.980
That means that Sasaura-<i>san</i> first stored the Aegis data on an online cloud service.

00:53:34.650 --> 00:53:37.940
And later, he copied it to the data card in his phone.

00:53:38.300 --> 00:53:43.030
But storing Aegis data on a cloud
 service aimed for public usage?

00:53:43.540 --> 00:53:46.320
Why would Sasaura-<i>san</i> do something like that?

00:53:46.320 --> 00:53:52.210
Doc, please use Sasaura-<i>san</i>'s ID to access the data on the cloud and send it to the captain's room.

00:53:52.210 --> 00:53:53.140
But how—

00:53:53.140 --> 00:53:54.300
It's okay.

00:53:54.300 --> 00:53:56.500
I just used it, and I remember the e-mail address.

00:53:56.960 --> 00:53:57.890
I'm counting on you.

00:54:02.980 --> 00:54:04.130
Sorry to ask you this right when you get here, but could you please tell us the results of your investigation.

00:54:04.130 --> 00:54:09.100
Sorry to ask you this right when you get here, but could you please tell us the results of your investigation.

00:54:09.620 --> 00:54:11.100
Of course.

00:54:11.100 --> 00:54:12.140
Captain...

00:54:12.140 --> 00:54:17.820
Before coming here, we investigated Sasaura-<i>han</i>'s last actions before his murder.

00:54:13.810 --> 00:54:16.810
Fumimaro Ayanokōji

00:54:13.810 --> 00:54:16.810
Kyōto Police Detective

00:54:13.810 --> 00:54:16.810
Kyōto Police Detective

00:54:13.810 --> 00:54:16.810
Detective Kurumazaki

00:54:18.630 --> 00:54:25.110
At 5:30 this morning, Sasaura-<i>han</i> was seen waving a Japanese flag on a cliff at Maizuru Harbour.

00:54:25.110 --> 00:54:27.200
An employee from a sightseeing cruise witnessed it.

00:54:27.740 --> 00:54:30.580
Why would Lt. Sasaura do such a thing?

00:54:30.580 --> 00:54:32.430
We don't know...

00:54:32.430 --> 00:54:34.620
But what happened yesterday is even more suspicious.

00:54:35.290 --> 00:54:39.710
You interrogated Sasaura-<i>han</i>
 at the Wakasa JMSDF base, right?

00:54:40.160 --> 00:54:41.090
Sekiguchi-<i>han</i>.

00:54:43.050 --> 00:54:46.010
Why did you question Sasaura-<i>han</i>?

00:54:46.010 --> 00:54:47.780
It's because...

00:54:49.000 --> 00:54:50.850
You're still hiding things?!

00:54:51.330 --> 00:54:55.570
Fujii-<i>san</i>, you can't even tell us?
 We're part of the JMSDF too!

00:54:55.570 --> 00:54:58.110
Unless we get approval from the Ministry of Defence...

00:54:58.110 --> 00:55:01.900
That's enough! Sasaura-<i>san</i> was murdered!

00:55:02.940 --> 00:55:06.880
We can't help you if you don't tell us the truth...

00:55:09.120 --> 00:55:12.450
He was part of your team, wasn't he?! Your friend was mu—

00:55:12.450 --> 00:55:13.700
That man was no friend of ours!

00:55:14.900 --> 00:55:16.360
If you don't mind explaining...

00:55:17.430 --> 00:55:18.420
What's this?

00:55:18.800 --> 00:55:21.050
Why is the data about the Aegis
 Destroyers being sent here...?

00:55:21.540 --> 00:55:22.370
Inspector.

00:55:22.370 --> 00:55:23.300
Right.

00:55:23.660 --> 00:55:27.010
If you won't cooperate willingly, then we'll have to force you.

00:55:29.050 --> 00:55:29.720
What's this...?

00:55:30.340 --> 00:55:33.930
It's being received under Sasaura-<i>san</i>'s ID from a cloud service, right?

00:55:33.930 --> 00:55:35.980
Nice timing, Doc!

00:55:35.980 --> 00:55:36.490
Cloud?

00:55:36.490 --> 00:55:39.270
It couldn't be to show it to X 
aboard this Aegis Destroyer, could it?

00:55:39.600 --> 00:55:40.740
Hold on!

00:55:40.740 --> 00:55:44.070
Storing data about Aegis Destroyers on the Internet is a breach of protocol!

00:55:45.250 --> 00:55:46.110
I see...

00:55:46.110 --> 00:55:49.490
That's why you questioned Sasaura-<i>han</i>...

00:55:50.520 --> 00:55:54.170
And that SDF lady knew about it too.

00:55:56.000 --> 00:55:57.080
Where are you going?!

00:55:58.840 --> 00:56:00.630
Hold on, we haven't fini—

00:56:00.630 --> 00:56:01.500
Let go!

00:56:02.200 --> 00:56:05.400
Unlike all of you, I work for the sake of this country!

00:56:09.600 --> 00:56:16.240
With that way of thinking, you won't be able to catch X, let alone protect your country.

00:56:18.790 --> 00:56:20.320
Let's work together.

00:56:21.350 --> 00:56:23.070
For Japan.

00:56:25.420 --> 00:56:29.280
Data about Aegis Destroyers has been being leaked from the Wakasa JMSDF base.

00:56:29.600 --> 00:56:31.160
Not another word, Lt. Sekiguchi!

00:56:32.370 --> 00:56:35.830
I was ordered to investigate it by Capt. Fujii!

00:56:37.730 --> 00:56:38.540
I thought so!

00:56:39.010 --> 00:56:43.190
Was it Lt. Sasaura who leaked the data about the Aegis Destroyers?

00:56:43.190 --> 00:56:43.940
Yes.

00:56:43.940 --> 00:56:47.670
Where did he send the data about the Aegis Destroyers to?

00:56:47.670 --> 00:56:53.290
To a detective agency run by a man called Takekawa, that ceased activity a few years ago.

00:56:53.290 --> 00:56:55.010
A shell company?

00:56:55.890 --> 00:57:00.450
The company was bought by a spy who called himself ‘Takekawa’.

00:57:00.450 --> 00:57:02.980
It's a common technique used by spies in Japan.

00:57:03.340 --> 00:57:08.070
And Sasaura-<i>san</i> was sending 
the intel to this ‘Takekawa’, right?

00:57:08.460 --> 00:57:09.130
Yes.

00:57:09.130 --> 00:57:10.490
The day after we discovered this fact,

00:57:11.440 --> 00:57:16.900
we were informed by the Coast Guard that a suspicious boat was found near Maizuru Harbour.

00:57:17.810 --> 00:57:21.310
A suspicious boat happening to appear near Maizuru Harbour, where this Aegis Destroyer was anchored...

00:57:21.310 --> 00:57:23.420
It couldn't have been a coincidence.

00:57:23.880 --> 00:57:27.050
And components from <i>that</i> country were found in the boat.

00:57:27.480 --> 00:57:28.200
Yeah.

00:57:28.200 --> 00:57:32.510
When we heard that, we figured a spy from the same country as Takekawa had arrived in Japan.

00:57:33.010 --> 00:57:34.030
 Don't tell me...

00:57:34.030 --> 00:57:35.140
 It was X?!

00:57:35.480 --> 00:57:41.430
We thought X might attempt to board this Destroyer with Lt. Sasaura's help.

00:57:41.430 --> 00:57:45.560
If so, it would likely be today, when the security would be lowered due to the sailing experience.

00:57:45.560 --> 00:57:48.860
Why didn't you say that in the first place?

00:57:49.800 --> 00:57:54.060
An SDF member might've leaked information about Aegis Destroyers to a foreign spy.

00:57:55.600 --> 00:57:58.830
Do you really think we could openly talk about such a huge scandal?

00:57:59.290 --> 00:58:03.540
We decided to investigate it on our own until we could find out the truth.

00:58:04.520 --> 00:58:07.340
So when I found his mobile phone on the deck...

00:58:10.390 --> 00:58:12.240
Did one of the civilians lose this?

00:58:15.230 --> 00:58:16.320
Why is this here?

00:58:17.230 --> 00:58:19.010
It's Lt. Sasaura's phone...

00:58:28.110 --> 00:58:29.820
Well then, let's begin our investigation on the deck...

00:58:33.800 --> 00:58:36.750
You found it before I did?

00:58:36.750 --> 00:58:40.820
Then Sasaura-<i>san</i> really <i>did</i> board this Aegis Destroyer.

00:58:40.820 --> 00:58:43.000
And was then murdered by X...

00:58:44.650 --> 00:58:48.160
Excuse me, I must contact the Ministry of Defence.

00:58:48.160 --> 00:58:51.050
You were the source of the satellite transmissions?!

00:58:51.050 --> 00:58:52.750
I apologise.

00:58:52.750 --> 00:58:56.260
But since you started worrying about it, I've been using it in the Degaussing Chamber.

00:58:57.650 --> 00:59:00.600
Phew, we must've almost bumped into each other...

00:59:00.600 --> 00:59:01.220
Fujii speaking.

00:59:01.650 --> 00:59:07.180
The police and Coast Guard found out about the classified case we were investigating...

00:59:08.850 --> 00:59:10.190
What? Takekawa?

00:59:11.190 --> 00:59:12.440
Around two hours ago...

00:59:12.830 --> 00:59:14.200
Yes...

00:59:14.200 --> 00:59:16.030
He was confirmed to have entered Kyōto.

00:59:16.950 --> 00:59:18.870
 They found Takekawa?!

00:59:16.950 --> 00:59:18.870
 Right, I'll do so now. I'll be in contact.

00:59:18.870 --> 00:59:22.230
 The fact that Takekawa came from Tōkyō to Kyōto means...

00:59:22.230 --> 00:59:25.250
 That he might be trying to meet up with X, who's aboard this ship.

00:59:25.250 --> 00:59:27.970
 Where's Takekawa now?

00:59:27.970 --> 00:59:31.150
Intelligence Security Command have entered Kyōto and are searching for him.

00:59:31.150 --> 00:59:33.840
 Then where was he spotted two hours ago?

00:59:34.180 --> 00:59:37.890
 He turned up on a surveillance camera in a hotel in Kyōto.

00:59:38.310 --> 00:59:41.380
 You have a photo of Takekawa, right?

00:59:41.380 --> 00:59:42.310
 Y-Yes...

00:59:42.310 --> 00:59:46.270
We can track him with the N System, Orbis, and outdoor surveillance cameras!

00:59:46.270 --> 00:59:50.230
 If that is your wish, the Kyōto Prefectural Police offers its full support.

00:59:50.580 --> 00:59:52.900
Please accept the help of the Coast Guard as well.

00:59:54.110 --> 00:59:57.940
 Please send the footage from all the cameras to this Destroyer.

00:59:58.640 --> 00:59:59.200
 I see!

00:59:59.780 --> 01:00:02.830
We can use the Aegis Destroyer Hotaka to quickly analyse all the footage!

01:00:03.270 --> 01:00:04.000
All right!

01:00:04.000 --> 01:00:06.460
See, things worked out pretty well!

01:00:07.560 --> 01:00:10.670
This is the footage from the cameras in Kyōto, two hours ago.

01:00:11.000 --> 01:00:15.490
I asked for footage from the cameras around the hotel where Takekawa was spotted to be sent first.

01:00:19.640 --> 01:00:21.090
A message from the Maizuru base!

01:00:21.680 --> 01:00:26.980
After towing the shipwreck, they found components from <i>that</i> country in the boat's structure.

01:00:27.600 --> 01:00:28.810
I'm putting it on the main monitor.

01:00:30.410 --> 01:00:32.650
It's from the same country as the one on the suspicious boat...

01:00:33.040 --> 01:00:36.610
But it's unthinkable for foreign ships to be passing through Japanese waters...

01:00:37.220 --> 01:00:43.450
In other words, this shipwreck approaching us can't have been a coincidence.

01:00:44.210 --> 01:00:45.060
 Don't tell me...

01:00:45.060 --> 01:00:47.850
Are you saying it's an act of terrorism using the tide?

01:00:47.850 --> 01:00:49.530
No, that can't be.

01:00:50.170 --> 01:00:55.840
This morning, before departure, we calculated the tides and the routes of the boats in the nearby area,

01:00:55.840 --> 01:00:59.100
and decided to change our planned route to the left.

01:00:59.100 --> 01:01:00.800
It was changed this morning?

01:01:00.800 --> 01:01:02.080
It was changed this morning...

01:01:02.080 --> 01:01:03.760
So the route...

01:01:04.340 --> 01:01:10.730
At 5:30 this morning, Sasaura-<i>han</i> was seen waving a Japanese flag on a cliff at Maizuru Harbour...

01:01:11.480 --> 01:01:13.190
Don't tell me that the reason for that was...

01:01:13.510 --> 01:01:14.580
I'll just have to check!

01:01:15.400 --> 01:01:17.480
This route change was decided this morning...

01:01:17.850 --> 01:01:22.530
Without knowing about it, it would have been impossible to target us so precisely with the shipwreck...

01:01:22.530 --> 01:01:23.070
Yes.

01:01:23.500 --> 01:01:26.360
Who knew about the change of route?

01:01:26.360 --> 01:01:28.370
 Only people from the Wakasa base.

01:01:28.370 --> 01:01:30.920
I see. So the spy couldn't have known about it.

01:01:30.920 --> 01:01:33.500
Wait, kid! Kid!

01:01:33.500 --> 01:01:34.890
Kid, you're coming here without permission again?

01:01:34.890 --> 01:01:35.710
You can't!

01:01:35.710 --> 01:01:37.160
What is it?

01:01:36.510 --> 01:01:37.920
I'm so sorry... He just ran past me...

01:01:37.160 --> 01:01:37.550
Is that it?!

01:01:38.340 --> 01:01:38.760
Hey!

01:01:39.390 --> 01:01:41.590
Don't come in here without permission!

01:01:42.220 --> 01:01:44.930
Oh? This isn't mine!

01:01:44.930 --> 01:01:46.670
Of course it's not!

01:01:46.670 --> 01:01:48.350
How many times do I have to tell you—

01:01:48.350 --> 01:01:49.010
Wait!

01:01:49.520 --> 01:01:53.850
You told us that only people from the Wakasa base knew about the change of route, right?

01:01:53.850 --> 01:01:54.750
Yes.

01:01:54.750 --> 01:01:57.480
Then Lt. Sasaura knew about it too.

01:01:58.570 --> 01:01:59.940
Look at this signal flag!

01:02:01.100 --> 01:02:06.120
In the dim early light of dawn, it wouldn't be hard to mistake it for the Japanese flag.

01:02:06.410 --> 01:02:07.520
Indeed.

01:02:07.520 --> 01:02:08.660
I see!

01:02:08.660 --> 01:02:12.880
Sasaura-<i>san</i> used this flag to send X a signal this morning!

01:02:12.880 --> 01:02:14.190
A signal?

01:02:14.190 --> 01:02:16.130
What does that flag mean?

01:02:17.100 --> 01:02:19.610
‘Change of route to the left’.

01:02:20.850 --> 01:02:21.610
Then...

01:02:21.610 --> 01:02:22.400
Yes.

01:02:22.400 --> 01:02:25.840
X knew about the change of route.

01:02:26.680 --> 01:02:29.280
Oh? I guess I must've left it somewhere else...

01:02:29.280 --> 01:02:30.810
I better get back to the cafeteria...

01:02:30.810 --> 01:02:32.420
Of course it's not here!

01:02:32.420 --> 01:02:33.190
Hold on, kid.

01:02:34.050 --> 01:02:34.960
 Crap...

01:02:34.960 --> 01:02:36.190
Target spotted!

01:02:36.190 --> 01:02:37.530
Really?

01:02:37.530 --> 01:02:38.400
Yes.

01:02:38.400 --> 01:02:40.790
It's a 93% match.

01:02:40.790 --> 01:02:42.110
It has to be Takekawa!

01:02:42.450 --> 01:02:43.490
Where is he?

01:02:43.490 --> 01:02:45.100
Ponto Town Park, Kyōto.

01:02:45.100 --> 01:02:46.930
 12:03 PM.

01:02:46.930 --> 01:02:47.910
 Zooming in!

01:02:54.850 --> 01:02:55.880
Ponto Town Park, right?

01:02:55.880 --> 01:02:56.980
Yeah, hurry there!

01:02:57.960 --> 01:03:00.300
If we don't hurry, they'll beat us there!

01:03:00.300 --> 01:03:01.600
Stop badgerin' me!

01:03:01.600 --> 01:03:04.050
 Oh, and get a picture of Takekawa too.

01:03:04.050 --> 01:03:05.250
A picture?

01:03:05.250 --> 01:03:06.380
 Why?

01:03:06.380 --> 01:03:06.980
I'm counting on you.

01:03:08.100 --> 01:03:09.330
 He hung up...

01:03:10.790 --> 01:03:11.950
 Anyway, hurry up!

01:03:11.950 --> 01:03:12.970
 Here we go!

01:03:15.190 --> 01:03:15.850
Crap...

01:03:15.850 --> 01:03:17.440
Conan-<i>kun</i> spotted!

01:03:18.730 --> 01:03:23.490
Where did you go? The treasure hunt's already started!

01:03:25.570 --> 01:03:26.450
 Target spotted!

01:03:27.150 --> 01:03:30.660
 12:10 PM, a platform at Gion-Shijō Station on the Keihan Main Line.

01:03:31.190 --> 01:03:33.370
That platform's for trains to Ōsaka, right?

01:03:33.370 --> 01:03:34.500
  Ah, he's getting in!

01:03:36.080 --> 01:03:37.050
It's an express train!

01:03:37.050 --> 01:03:38.960
So there won't be many stations it stops at.

01:03:39.490 --> 01:03:41.880
 I'll ask the Ōsaka Police to cooperate.

01:03:44.840 --> 01:03:46.800
The kid's gone...

01:03:46.800 --> 01:03:49.760
Ōsaka Police HQ

01:03:48.220 --> 01:03:49.760
Please send all surveillance footage

01:03:49.760 --> 01:03:56.670
from cameras at stations served by express trains on the Keihan Main Line between Gion-Shijō and Yodoyabashi to this location.

01:03:56.670 --> 01:03:59.190
The CIC of the Aegis Destroyer Hotaka?

01:03:59.850 --> 01:04:00.770
 I'm counting on you, Ōtaki.

01:04:00.770 --> 01:04:02.380
 It's urgent!

01:04:02.380 --> 01:04:02.980
 Yes, sir!

01:04:02.980 --> 01:04:08.880
 For this treasure hunt, we've hidden five types of items around the cafeteria and the front half of the deck.

01:04:08.880 --> 01:04:10.700
 Try and find them all!

01:04:11.200 --> 01:04:12.160
 Found one!

01:04:12.160 --> 01:04:14.130
 Guys, I got one!

01:04:14.130 --> 01:04:16.070
 Cool!

01:04:16.070 --> 01:04:17.280
 Congratulations.

01:04:17.280 --> 01:04:18.960
 That's the third one.

01:04:18.960 --> 01:04:20.850
 So there's only two remaining.

01:04:20.850 --> 01:04:22.590
 Let's find them quickly and get to the deck.

01:04:25.150 --> 01:04:27.050
Ran, come help us!

01:04:27.050 --> 01:04:27.880
Right.

01:04:30.840 --> 01:04:32.350
 The discovery of a suspicious boat...

01:04:34.310 --> 01:04:35.930
 The sudden switch into combat...

01:04:37.770 --> 01:04:39.900
 And Sasaura-<i>san</i>'s death...

01:04:42.090 --> 01:04:45.480
If they were all the work of <i>that</i> country's spy, ‘X’...

01:04:45.880 --> 01:04:50.280
We believe he is trying to obtain classified intel on Aegis Destroyers.

01:04:52.100 --> 01:04:52.950
 Kid...

01:04:53.410 --> 01:04:54.910
 Can I ask you something?

01:04:54.910 --> 01:04:57.870
Ponto Town Park

01:04:58.250 --> 01:04:59.850
Something smells burnt.

01:04:59.850 --> 01:05:00.580
 Yeah.

01:05:01.190 --> 01:05:03.420
 This must be what Kudō asked us to find.

01:05:05.850 --> 01:05:06.990
 The police are here.

01:05:13.680 --> 01:05:14.970
 Found it, there it is!

01:05:15.470 --> 01:05:17.410
Okay, report it in quickly!

01:05:17.410 --> 01:05:18.060
 Right!

01:05:19.520 --> 01:05:20.390
Conan-<i>kun</i>...

01:05:21.140 --> 01:05:22.930
 You did a great job back then.

01:05:22.930 --> 01:05:24.110
Huh? What do you mean?

01:05:25.940 --> 01:05:27.570
Just who are you?

01:05:29.350 --> 01:05:33.030
Just what kind of data can only be obtained on this ship?

01:05:33.950 --> 01:05:37.370
Is it data about situations like what would happen if a submarine suddenly attacks?

01:05:38.600 --> 01:05:40.340
How do you know about...

01:05:40.340 --> 01:05:41.390
That's what I thought...

01:05:43.270 --> 01:05:47.570
Do you mean X sent us the shipwreck to get this data?

01:05:47.570 --> 01:05:50.130
Where can the data be accessed?

01:05:50.130 --> 01:05:52.510
In the CIC we were just in...

01:05:52.510 --> 01:05:54.340
...and in the captain's quarters.

01:05:55.320 --> 01:05:56.210
That's it!

01:05:57.040 --> 01:06:02.050
During the training, the captain came to the CIC because of the sudden emergency.

01:06:03.690 --> 01:06:05.980
So there was nobody in the captain's quarters at the time.

01:06:05.980 --> 01:06:07.590
I see.

01:06:07.590 --> 01:06:10.610
So that's when X went into the captain's quarters and stole the data!

01:06:11.710 --> 01:06:13.610
Then X is that person!

01:06:15.340 --> 01:06:16.660
Hold on!

01:06:18.390 --> 01:06:19.120
Conan-<i>kun</i>!

01:06:19.700 --> 01:06:22.060
That brat again?

01:06:22.060 --> 01:06:23.920
I'm a bit worried, so I'm going after him.

01:06:24.700 --> 01:06:26.960
W-Wait, Ran!

01:06:28.310 --> 01:06:29.890
Wait, kid!

01:06:29.890 --> 01:06:30.750
Capt. Fujii!

01:06:31.990 --> 01:06:34.380
Takekawa entered Ōsaka!

01:06:34.380 --> 01:06:35.140
Ōsaka?

01:06:35.140 --> 01:06:37.200
Yes, at Yodoyabashi Station.

01:06:41.210 --> 01:06:42.350
Kudō?

01:06:42.350 --> 01:06:44.890
What Takekawa threw away is some kind of memo.

01:06:45.470 --> 01:06:46.550
A memo?

01:06:46.550 --> 01:06:50.860
Yeah. Most of it is burnt though, so I can't read it.

01:06:50.860 --> 01:06:52.650
It seems Takekawa went to Yodoyabashi Station in Ōsaka.

01:06:52.650 --> 01:06:56.200
It seems Takekawa went to Yodoyabashi Station in Ōsaka.

01:06:56.200 --> 01:06:57.440
Go after him!

01:06:57.440 --> 01:06:58.120
Gotcha!

01:07:11.240 --> 01:07:13.320
Yūki-<i>kun</i>. Yūki-<i>kun</i>.

01:07:19.910 --> 01:07:22.110
Amemiya-<i>san</i>? Amemiya-<i>san</i>!

01:07:23.430 --> 01:07:24.560
Amemiya-<i>san</i>!

01:07:26.010 --> 01:07:26.890
Oh, it's you.

01:07:26.890 --> 01:07:29.440
Hey, is Yūki-<i>kun</i> okay?

01:07:30.400 --> 01:07:32.170
Now that you mention it, where is Yūki...

01:07:32.170 --> 01:07:35.280
He told me he went to the toilet because his eczema flared up.

01:07:35.280 --> 01:07:37.110
Oh, his eczema.

01:07:37.110 --> 01:07:37.660
Yeah.

01:07:37.660 --> 01:07:41.490
When that happens, he has to wash his hands and put on some cream, right?

01:07:41.490 --> 01:07:43.530
Y-Yeah.

01:07:43.530 --> 01:07:44.450
So he's in the toilet...

01:07:45.050 --> 01:07:46.540
Are you worried about Yūki-<i>kun</i>?

01:07:46.540 --> 01:07:48.170
Of course I am.

01:07:48.540 --> 01:07:52.630
But when the boat shook, you weren't with him...

01:07:55.140 --> 01:07:57.650
I told you I was in the toilet!

01:07:57.650 --> 01:07:59.840
No, you were in the captain's quarters.

01:08:00.800 --> 01:08:04.060
You didn't react when I called you Amemiya-<i>san</i> either.

01:08:04.690 --> 01:08:08.440
And Yūki-<i>kun</i> isn't carrying medical cream, but pills.

01:08:09.520 --> 01:08:12.520
And they're not for eczema, but food allergies.

01:08:12.920 --> 01:08:15.660
There's no way his father wouldn't know something like that.

01:08:15.660 --> 01:08:19.060
In other words, you're not Yūki-<i>kun</i>'s father.

01:08:19.060 --> 01:08:20.380
Isn't that right?

01:08:20.380 --> 01:08:21.620
Mr. Foreign Spy.

01:08:24.150 --> 01:08:25.950
Who the hell are you?

01:08:27.650 --> 01:08:28.700
Conan Edogawa...

01:08:30.360 --> 01:08:31.380
Detective.

01:08:34.280 --> 01:08:35.460
You're just a kid.

01:08:35.850 --> 01:08:37.300
What can you do?

01:08:49.760 --> 01:08:51.270
You okay, kid?

01:08:56.130 --> 01:08:56.900
Wait!

01:08:56.900 --> 01:08:57.440
Stop!

01:08:58.820 --> 01:08:59.680
Stop!

01:08:59.680 --> 01:09:01.030
My dad'll be killed!

01:09:07.500 --> 01:09:10.830
Damn it, old man...

01:09:14.110 --> 01:09:16.500
This is the only part I could make readable.

01:09:16.500 --> 01:09:18.330
Senshu...

01:09:18.330 --> 01:09:19.220
What's that at the end?

01:09:19.700 --> 01:09:25.060
senshu

01:09:19.700 --> 01:09:25.060
If it's related to an Aegis Destroyer, isn't it the bow of the boat?

01:09:25.060 --> 01:09:26.970
And if it's about boats, isn't that an anchor?

01:09:26.970 --> 01:09:30.520
No! The bottom half of an anchor sign is longer!

01:09:30.960 --> 01:09:33.150
It looks more like an arrow than an anchor.

01:09:33.820 --> 01:09:35.980
An arrow?

01:09:36.430 --> 01:09:39.180
Like an arrow telling you to look up at the sky?

01:09:39.180 --> 01:09:40.200
The sky?

01:09:40.990 --> 01:09:41.910
Oh, I got it!

01:09:42.300 --> 01:09:45.070
Kazuha! That was a great idea!

01:09:46.190 --> 01:09:47.040
A great idea?

01:09:47.460 --> 01:09:49.850
Hey, pops, it's Senshu Airport!

01:09:49.850 --> 01:09:50.970
What?

01:09:50.970 --> 01:09:52.790
This isn't an anchor or an arrow.

01:09:53.360 --> 01:09:54.440
It's an aeroplane!

01:09:54.440 --> 01:09:55.250
An aeroplane?

01:09:55.250 --> 01:09:57.890
Is there even a Senshu Airport?

01:09:57.890 --> 01:10:00.220
It's also known as Kansai International Airport...

01:10:00.220 --> 01:10:03.930
Kansai Airport used to be called ‘Senshu Airport’!

01:10:04.600 --> 01:10:10.890
He told me that his father vanished at Maizuru Harbour before departure, and he boarded the ship with a man he didn't know.

01:10:11.200 --> 01:10:15.490
He said he'd kill Dad if I didn't do what he said.

01:10:15.490 --> 01:10:18.860
The man who wasn't with us in
 the CIC during the training, right?

01:10:19.370 --> 01:10:23.540
He had to be stealing the training data from the captain's quarters.

01:10:23.540 --> 01:10:25.530
Which means he's X.

01:10:25.860 --> 01:10:28.170
Do you remember his face?

01:10:28.850 --> 01:10:29.490
Yes.

01:10:30.050 --> 01:10:31.510
Will you help us?

01:10:32.560 --> 01:10:33.830
I will!

01:10:33.830 --> 01:10:35.210
I remember his face!

01:10:35.660 --> 01:10:39.500
Then come with us to look at the surveillance camera footage in the CIC.

01:10:39.500 --> 01:10:40.170
Okay!

01:10:40.170 --> 01:10:42.400
Let's go.

01:10:42.400 --> 01:10:43.650
Let's go, little boy.

01:10:46.810 --> 01:10:50.600
Your dad told you why he named you Yūki, didn't he?

01:10:51.600 --> 01:10:52.810
yūki

01:10:51.600 --> 01:10:52.810
So be brave and do your best.

01:10:55.170 --> 01:10:56.730
Takekawa and X...

01:10:57.040 --> 01:10:59.180
It seems we haven't been able to catch either of them yet.

01:10:59.180 --> 01:11:00.070
I see.

01:11:00.070 --> 01:11:01.890
It's Kansai Airport!

01:11:01.890 --> 01:11:03.950
There's a high chance Takekawa went to Kansai Airport.

01:11:04.290 --> 01:11:05.100
What?

01:11:05.100 --> 01:11:06.410
How do you know that?

01:11:06.410 --> 01:11:07.940
Well, Hei-<i>chan</i>...

01:11:07.940 --> 01:11:08.950
I mean, your son...

01:11:08.950 --> 01:11:10.230
Heiji?

01:11:10.230 --> 01:11:10.660
Then?

01:11:10.660 --> 01:11:13.620
I tried to stop him but he's already heading there.

01:11:13.620 --> 01:11:16.780
Tōyama, set up an emergency deployment at Kansai Airport.

01:11:16.780 --> 01:11:18.590
Ōtaki, you meet up with the Kansai Airport police!

01:11:19.030 --> 01:11:20.250
Don't let him get away!

01:11:28.430 --> 01:11:29.050
Here it is...

01:11:32.160 --> 01:11:33.730
And where did Takekawa go after that?

01:11:34.130 --> 01:11:36.310
We last spotted him at Namba Station. Nothing after that.

01:11:36.310 --> 01:11:37.350
Is that so?

01:11:37.770 --> 01:11:39.570
What about the eyewitness for X?

01:11:39.570 --> 01:11:42.960
Conan-<i>kun</i> ended up helping us with that.

01:11:44.230 --> 01:11:46.550
Okay, sit here and check the monitor.

01:11:46.550 --> 01:11:47.580
Okay!

01:11:47.580 --> 01:11:49.530
How come <i>he</i> knows X?

01:11:49.980 --> 01:11:53.500
Tell me if you see the man from before on the monitor.

01:11:53.500 --> 01:11:54.100
Yes...

01:11:54.730 --> 01:11:56.620
No, the footage is disappearing!

01:11:56.960 --> 01:11:57.970
What?

01:11:57.970 --> 01:12:00.750
This is footage stored in the server room.

01:12:00.750 --> 01:12:01.630
What is it?

01:12:01.630 --> 01:12:04.460
He got us. He must've deleted the footage from the server.

01:12:02.080 --> 01:12:04.460
Damn, he beat us to it.

01:12:04.460 --> 01:12:06.350
Don't you have any other footage?

01:12:06.350 --> 01:12:08.950
We can still monitor the real-time camera footage.

01:12:08.950 --> 01:12:10.020
Switch to those, now!

01:12:10.020 --> 01:12:10.390
Right.

01:12:10.780 --> 01:12:12.650
Just hold on for a bit, kid.

01:12:14.000 --> 01:12:17.660
I doubt X would screw up and expose himself to a camera at this point.

01:12:18.350 --> 01:12:22.080
The only thing we can do now is ask Yūki-<i>kun</i> about the routes X tended to use.

01:12:22.080 --> 01:12:23.440
A message from the Ōsaka Police.

01:12:23.440 --> 01:12:27.570
There's a high possibility that Takekawa's headed for Kansai International Airport.

01:12:28.000 --> 01:12:28.560
What?

01:12:28.560 --> 01:12:31.030
Is he planning to escape on a plane in plain sight?

01:12:32.180 --> 01:12:37.170
We apologise, but we have to
 stop the treasure hunt on the deck.

01:12:37.170 --> 01:12:40.850
We will continue it in the cafeteria, so please head back inside.

01:12:39.350 --> 01:12:41.770
Where did Conan-<i>kun</i> go?

01:12:41.770 --> 01:12:46.130
Sorry, the waves are getting
 rougher, so please head back inside.

01:12:46.130 --> 01:12:49.040
Have you seen a boy wearing glasses?

01:12:49.040 --> 01:12:50.180
A lost kid?

01:12:50.180 --> 01:12:53.360
No, it's not like that...

01:12:53.360 --> 01:12:55.510
Then please get back inside...

01:12:55.510 --> 01:12:57.050
We're sealing off the deck.

01:12:57.050 --> 01:12:58.140
R-Right...

01:12:58.870 --> 01:13:00.600
It seems Takekawa's heading to Kansai Airport.

01:13:01.330 --> 01:13:04.700
I'm going to ask the Coast Guard base at Kansai Airport for their cooperation.

01:13:05.770 --> 01:13:07.960
Inoue-<i>san</i>, I leave the rest to you.

01:13:07.960 --> 01:13:08.440
Right.

01:13:10.120 --> 01:13:12.660
Now we just have to find X in this ship...

01:13:13.410 --> 01:13:17.120
Your dad told you why he named you Yūki, didn't he?

01:13:18.080 --> 01:13:19.330
yūki

01:13:18.080 --> 01:13:19.330
So be brave and do your best.

01:13:22.330 --> 01:13:22.790
I...

01:13:24.690 --> 01:13:27.090
I want to help catch the spy too!

01:13:28.480 --> 01:13:29.800
Target spotted at Kansai Airport!

01:13:30.740 --> 01:13:32.760
It's a 89% match!

01:13:33.280 --> 01:13:34.650
The North Wing of the terminal.

01:13:34.650 --> 01:13:36.600
This is footage from the surveillance camera outside gate #3.

01:13:37.110 --> 01:13:38.850
He's heading into the airport.

01:13:39.650 --> 01:13:41.820
We'll be there soon, Yūki-<i>kun</i>.

01:13:45.650 --> 01:13:47.750
Excuse me, can I ask you something?

01:13:47.750 --> 01:13:48.610
Yes. What is it?

01:13:49.150 --> 01:13:51.150
Could it be... You're X—!

01:13:56.040 --> 01:13:57.410
What is it, Yūki?

01:13:57.900 --> 01:14:02.080
Did you think I'd just let you go, when you know my travel routes?

01:14:03.580 --> 01:14:04.380
Stand up!

01:14:05.050 --> 01:14:06.840
Hurry and stand up!

01:14:11.670 --> 01:14:14.170
Geez, that Conan-<i>kun</i>!

01:14:14.170 --> 01:14:16.950
Next time I find him, I'm never going to let him go about freely again.

01:14:18.100 --> 01:14:19.850
Huh? Is that Yūki-<i>kun</i> and his dad?

01:14:20.250 --> 01:14:23.300
Didn't they know the deck's off-limits?

01:14:30.300 --> 01:14:32.150
Are you sure he's here?

01:14:32.150 --> 01:14:35.110
Yes, Takekawa's definitely here.

01:14:35.110 --> 01:14:37.850
Then we'll follow you after we park the car.

01:14:37.850 --> 01:14:39.390
Okay, we'll go ahead.

01:14:39.390 --> 01:14:41.830
Hey! Wait, Heiji!

01:14:42.550 --> 01:14:43.980
Why are we here?

01:14:43.980 --> 01:14:47.700
The police know Takekawa's face now.

01:14:47.700 --> 01:14:49.800
He can't mix in with the regular passengers.

01:14:50.200 --> 01:14:52.150
Where did you get this picture?

01:14:52.150 --> 01:14:54.010
I made Ōtaki-<i>han</i> send it to me.

01:14:55.290 --> 01:14:57.970
So the only way to board a plane without exposing his face is... freight.

01:14:58.690 --> 01:15:02.200
In other words, the only thing he can do is hide in the international freight.

01:15:02.200 --> 01:15:03.550
Hey, kids!

01:15:03.550 --> 01:15:05.190
This place is dangerous, move it!

01:15:05.190 --> 01:15:06.010
Right!

01:15:17.150 --> 01:15:19.800
We're waiting here until the next patrol comes.

01:15:19.800 --> 01:15:20.450
Got it?

01:15:21.410 --> 01:15:24.510
If you stay quiet, you'll get to meet your father.

01:15:24.510 --> 01:15:25.500
Excuse me!

01:15:25.500 --> 01:15:27.460
Have you seen Conan-<i>kun</i>?

01:15:27.980 --> 01:15:31.420
He's the boy with glasses who was with me.

01:15:32.640 --> 01:15:34.630
No, we haven't seen him.

01:15:34.950 --> 01:15:36.350
Is that so?

01:15:36.350 --> 01:15:37.590
You haven't seen him either, Yūki-<i>kun</i>?

01:15:38.990 --> 01:15:42.560
Yūki was with me, so I doubt he saw him.

01:15:43.100 --> 01:15:45.550
Lost kids really are a bother, huh?

01:15:45.550 --> 01:15:47.040
Isn't that right.

01:15:47.040 --> 01:15:48.540
See you later, Yūki-<i>kun</i>.

01:15:49.290 --> 01:15:51.070
Geez, he's always disappearing...

01:15:55.530 --> 01:15:58.700
Oh, I forgot to tell you but this place is off-limits!

01:15:59.020 --> 01:16:00.400
Really?

01:16:00.400 --> 01:16:03.680
Then we'll head back in once Yūki's seasickness is over.

01:16:05.030 --> 01:16:06.330
Miss, save me!

01:16:06.770 --> 01:16:08.170
This man is a spy!

01:16:08.170 --> 01:16:09.330
Yūki!

01:16:09.830 --> 01:16:12.040
Do you really think you can do that?

01:16:12.610 --> 01:16:14.150
What is it, Yūki-<i>kun</i>?

01:16:14.150 --> 01:16:15.290
Are you okay?

01:16:15.290 --> 01:16:16.670
Excuse us.

01:16:17.040 --> 01:16:21.500
We kept playing spies so I guess it got to his head...

01:16:21.500 --> 01:16:22.560
That's not it!

01:16:22.560 --> 01:16:24.560
This man isn't my father!

01:16:25.110 --> 01:16:26.330
Not your father?

01:16:28.150 --> 01:16:30.650
Then you stay with him, Conan-<i>kun</i>.

01:16:30.650 --> 01:16:33.650
I'll talk to an SDF member about Yūki-<i>kun</i>'s situation.

01:16:33.950 --> 01:16:36.110
Stop. If you do that...

01:16:36.800 --> 01:16:37.990
If I do that...?

01:16:39.360 --> 01:16:41.450
I'm fine.

01:16:42.310 --> 01:16:44.160
He really isn't your father, is he?

01:16:44.630 --> 01:16:46.190
No, he's not!

01:16:46.190 --> 01:16:47.500
Save me, Miss!

01:16:47.500 --> 01:16:49.120
Enough, Yūki!

01:16:49.120 --> 01:16:50.450
Yūki-<i>kun</i>, come here!

01:16:55.360 --> 01:16:57.010
Stupid girl.

01:16:57.010 --> 01:16:59.760
If you'd minded your own business, you wouldn't have to die!

01:16:59.760 --> 01:17:02.530
So you really <i>are</i> a spy.

01:17:02.530 --> 01:17:03.800
I am...

01:17:04.270 --> 01:17:07.090
But it's too late for you to have regrets.

01:17:10.750 --> 01:17:11.440
What?

01:17:19.670 --> 01:17:21.880
Yūki-<i>kun</i>, call everybody!

01:17:21.880 --> 01:17:22.450
OK.

01:17:24.210 --> 01:17:25.660
Brat.

01:17:27.080 --> 01:17:28.910
I won't let him go!

01:17:41.250 --> 01:17:42.750
Figures.

01:17:42.750 --> 01:17:43.090
But...

01:18:22.460 --> 01:18:23.720
Target spotted.

01:18:23.720 --> 01:18:25.300
He's at the International Freight Section G.

01:18:25.700 --> 01:18:26.430
Okay.

01:18:26.430 --> 01:18:27.650
You're sure about it?

01:18:27.650 --> 01:18:30.520
Yes, it's a 97% match.

01:18:30.520 --> 01:18:32.480
I'm counting on you, Hattori.

01:18:32.480 --> 01:18:34.690
Hello? This is Megure from the Tōkyō Police.

01:18:34.690 --> 01:18:37.370
We spotted Takekawa in Section G.

01:18:37.370 --> 01:18:37.900
Okay.

01:18:37.900 --> 01:18:39.900
Takekawa's in Section G.

01:18:39.900 --> 01:18:41.100
Section G's this way.

01:18:45.830 --> 01:18:47.460
Oh, you can't go in there.

01:18:47.460 --> 01:18:48.330
Let me go!

01:18:48.330 --> 01:18:50.200
Kid, you can't go in there.

01:18:50.200 --> 01:18:52.000
Let me go!

01:18:52.000 --> 01:18:52.410
Stop!

01:18:52.750 --> 01:18:54.120
I told you to let me go!

01:18:54.120 --> 01:18:54.750
Yūki-<i>kun</i>!

01:18:54.750 --> 01:18:56.150
The spy!

01:18:56.150 --> 01:18:56.710
What?!

01:18:56.710 --> 01:18:58.670
The spy was there!

01:18:59.350 --> 01:19:03.490
With a face like this, he could be anywhere! How am I supposed to find him?

01:19:03.490 --> 01:19:04.970
Hey, watch out!

01:19:08.140 --> 01:19:09.280
You okay?

01:19:10.570 --> 01:19:11.810
Thanks...

01:19:11.810 --> 01:19:14.100
Don't be so stupid.

01:19:14.600 --> 01:19:16.350
Wanderin' around alone like that's dangerous.

01:19:16.350 --> 01:19:18.390
Wait for me here, okay?

01:19:19.940 --> 01:19:21.350
I'll be back soon!

01:19:21.350 --> 01:19:22.820
Hey, Heiji!

01:19:24.100 --> 01:19:28.280
If that's how you're gonna be, I'll show you! I'll find Takekawa before you!

01:19:32.740 --> 01:19:34.770
T-Takekawa?!

01:19:37.580 --> 01:19:42.930
Wait, Takekawa! Wait! You won't get away!

01:19:42.930 --> 01:19:45.300
What is it, Kazuha? Kazuha!

01:19:45.300 --> 01:19:45.930
Where did you go?

01:19:47.000 --> 01:19:48.970
Don't tell me she went off on her own!

01:19:51.530 --> 01:19:52.600
There!

01:19:52.600 --> 01:19:53.660
It's him!

01:19:56.030 --> 01:19:58.310
This is the police! Stop!

01:19:58.630 --> 01:19:59.440
Move!

01:19:59.870 --> 01:20:00.360
Stop!

01:20:01.670 --> 01:20:02.950
Wait, Nanami-<i>san</i>!

01:20:04.080 --> 01:20:04.860
Let's go to the deck.

01:20:06.050 --> 01:20:10.780
A spy who had his identity exposed isn't going to wait aboard the ship until we reach the harbour.

01:20:11.720 --> 01:20:12.160
You're right.

01:20:12.680 --> 01:20:14.450
But you two...

01:20:14.450 --> 01:20:15.600
Wait, Conan-<i>kun</i>!

01:20:15.600 --> 01:20:17.620
Yūki-<i>kun</i>, go back to where everyone is. Okay?

01:20:18.800 --> 01:20:21.710
But that lady...

01:20:22.160 --> 01:20:23.670
Wait!

01:20:43.820 --> 01:20:45.280
Don't come any closer!

01:20:45.280 --> 01:20:47.320
Not one more step!

01:20:47.320 --> 01:20:48.440
Give yourself up!

01:20:48.440 --> 01:20:49.700
You have nowhere to run!

01:20:50.680 --> 01:20:52.320
You sure about that?

01:20:53.170 --> 01:20:54.700
Don't do anything stupid!

01:21:00.940 --> 01:21:02.460
There's too many obstacles in the way.

01:21:03.350 --> 01:21:04.420
It's almost vertical.

01:21:04.980 --> 01:21:06.520
I can't shoot my ball at that angle.

01:21:10.800 --> 01:21:11.750
There!

01:21:11.750 --> 01:21:12.220
Nanami-<i>san</i>!

01:21:13.080 --> 01:21:15.810
Can you rotate that cannon anticlockwise?

01:21:15.810 --> 01:21:16.850
The cannon?

01:21:16.850 --> 01:21:18.520
If you can, do it right now!

01:21:18.900 --> 01:21:19.890
Please!

01:21:29.320 --> 01:21:31.940
Kazuha!

01:21:31.940 --> 01:21:32.410
Die!

01:21:33.110 --> 01:21:34.870
Hei... ji...

01:21:35.770 --> 01:21:36.990
Get down!

01:21:47.200 --> 01:21:49.230
You okay, Hei-<i>chan</i>?!

01:21:55.720 --> 01:21:56.770
Stop!

01:21:57.680 --> 01:21:58.670
You're not getting away!

01:22:01.350 --> 01:22:02.560
Don't move!

01:22:11.950 --> 01:22:14.620
Go!

01:22:23.100 --> 01:22:23.710
No way!

01:22:32.090 --> 01:22:33.470
Suspect arrested!

01:22:33.470 --> 01:22:35.000
Give yourself up, Takekawa!

01:22:35.000 --> 01:22:37.000
Okay, I'll leave the rest to you.

01:22:37.000 --> 01:22:38.910
You okay, Hei-<i>chan</i>?

01:22:38.910 --> 01:22:41.630
Hurry up, call an ambulance!

01:22:41.630 --> 01:22:42.940
Don't be so dramatic...

01:22:42.940 --> 01:22:43.720
Heiji!

01:22:43.720 --> 01:22:46.270
I'm fine, it's just a scratch.

01:22:46.270 --> 01:22:47.750
Really, Hei-<i>chan</i>?

01:22:47.750 --> 01:22:48.510
Yeah.

01:22:49.460 --> 01:22:51.240
What is it, Kazuha?

01:22:51.240 --> 01:22:51.920
Oh, crap.

01:22:51.920 --> 01:22:52.750
Don't cry!

01:22:57.670 --> 01:22:59.270
Ouch!

01:22:59.270 --> 01:23:00.330
I just got shot there, you know!

01:23:02.730 --> 01:23:04.060
Let go! Lemme go!

01:23:05.580 --> 01:23:07.210
Ouch!

01:23:11.680 --> 01:23:13.820
I was getting a bit nervous there.

01:23:14.520 --> 01:23:15.680
But now it's case clos—

01:23:15.680 --> 01:23:16.400
Inspector!

01:23:16.400 --> 01:23:17.390
Please look at this.

01:23:17.390 --> 01:23:24.730
The Kansai Airport Police informed us that they found a pressurised room disguised as a healing capsule among the international freight.

01:23:24.730 --> 01:23:26.940
So he planned to escape in that.

01:23:26.940 --> 01:23:35.150
Also, after seizing Takekawa at Kansai Airport, they found a suspicious voicemail, so I asked them to send it to us.

01:23:35.150 --> 01:23:37.960
Play that voicemail as soon as you can.

01:23:37.960 --> 01:23:39.950
It might be a message from Lt. Sasaura.

01:23:40.340 --> 01:23:42.650
Got it. I'll set it up.

01:23:46.600 --> 01:23:47.850
Yummy!

01:23:47.850 --> 01:23:49.040
Say...

01:23:49.040 --> 01:23:50.360
What is it?

01:23:50.360 --> 01:23:50.840
Are you lost?

01:23:51.180 --> 01:23:53.370
Where is the lady who was with you?

01:23:53.370 --> 01:23:54.990
You mean Ran?

01:23:55.880 --> 01:23:57.690
Now that you mention it, where <i>is</i> Ran-<i>oneesan</i>?

01:23:57.690 --> 01:24:00.070
She's still looking for Conan-<i>kun</i>.

01:24:00.510 --> 01:24:05.180
The access ID is ‘aegis0902’.

01:24:05.900 --> 01:24:09.280
The password is ‘0505informer’.

01:24:09.930 --> 01:24:12.400
There's no doubt about it, that's Lt. Sasaura's voice.

01:24:10.200 --> 01:24:15.390
Message recorded on April 20th, at 5:30 AM.

01:24:15.390 --> 01:24:18.220
That's Sasaura-<i>san</i>'s estimated time of death.

01:24:18.220 --> 01:24:21.220
This voicemail was on Takekawa's phone.

01:24:21.220 --> 01:24:25.870
This is definitive proof that Lt. Sasaura sent the data about the Aegis Destroyers to Takekawa.

01:24:25.870 --> 01:24:27.380
We could hear the waves too, right?

01:24:28.230 --> 01:24:30.640
So maybe he was somewhere near the sea.

01:24:30.640 --> 01:24:32.150
Waves?

01:24:32.150 --> 01:24:34.090
And we can hear someone else talking too.

01:24:34.850 --> 01:24:36.180
Play it again!

01:24:36.180 --> 01:24:36.930
Right.

01:24:37.920 --> 01:24:41.800
I saved the Aegis data on the KRY Cloud.

01:24:41.800 --> 01:24:46.950
The access ID is ‘aegis0902’.

01:24:46.950 --> 01:24:50.760
The password is ‘0505informer’.

01:24:48.480 --> 01:24:49.980
What's that metallic sound?

01:24:51.050 --> 01:24:52.720
Play the last part again.

01:24:52.720 --> 01:24:53.690
Right.

01:24:54.370 --> 01:24:57.650
The password is ‘0505informer’.

01:24:57.650 --> 01:24:59.690
 It's true, you can hear something.

01:24:59.690 --> 01:25:00.890
It's a man's voice.

01:25:00.890 --> 01:25:03.140
But we can't understand what he's saying.

01:25:03.140 --> 01:25:04.900
I'll send it for analysis.

01:25:04.900 --> 01:25:06.120
Thank you.

01:25:06.600 --> 01:25:08.750
What's this uneasy feeling I have?

01:25:08.750 --> 01:25:10.810
It's like there's something still left unsolved...

01:25:16.570 --> 01:25:17.800
Is that you, Shin'ichi?

01:25:17.800 --> 01:25:22.850
The TBT we found on Sasaura-<i>san</i>'s body isn't from the Aegis Destroyer Hotaka.

01:25:25.590 --> 01:25:27.220
But it <i>is</i> boat paint, right?

01:25:27.530 --> 01:25:32.190
Yes. After checking the ships arriving and departing from Maizuru Harbour and Wakasa Harbour,

01:25:32.530 --> 01:25:37.420
we found out that one of the sightseeing cruises passing by the old naval port

01:25:37.420 --> 01:25:40.200
left Maizuru Harbour and passed by Wakasa Shipyard today.

01:25:40.530 --> 01:25:45.280
As expected, the paint on that sightseeing cruise matched with the TBT.

01:25:45.760 --> 01:25:52.960
Then Sasaura-<i>san</i>'s body was dragged along by that sightseeing cruise and moved from Maizuru Harbour to Wakasa Harbour?

01:25:53.360 --> 01:25:55.590
Yes, there's no doubt about it.

01:25:55.590 --> 01:25:59.740
A sightseeing cruise departing from Maizuru Harbour?

01:25:59.740 --> 01:26:05.710
At 5:30 this morning, Sasaura-<i>han</i> was seen waving a Japanese flag on a cliff at Maizuru Harbour.

01:26:05.720 --> 01:26:08.140
An employee from a sightseeing cruise witnessed it.

01:26:08.140 --> 01:26:09.300
The password is ‘05—

01:26:09.310 --> 01:26:13.560
Message recorded on April 20th, at 5:30 AM.

01:26:13.560 --> 01:26:16.400
His watch stopped at 5:30 AM.

01:26:16.400 --> 01:26:19.360
And the last call was this morning at 5:30.

01:26:19.360 --> 01:26:20.990
5:30 this morning?

01:26:20.990 --> 01:26:23.020
That's when his wristwatch stopped.

01:26:23.030 --> 01:26:25.240
It's also his estimated time of death.

01:26:28.460 --> 01:26:31.360
The time the witness saw Sasaura-<i>san</i>...

01:26:31.360 --> 01:26:32.700
The time he left the voicemail...

01:26:33.370 --> 01:26:34.630
The time he died...

01:26:34.630 --> 01:26:37.000
They were all at the same time!

01:26:37.000 --> 01:26:37.960
5:30!

01:26:38.760 --> 01:26:42.220
Oh, I see! I made a huge mistake!

01:26:52.600 --> 01:26:55.020
After having been arrested at Kansai Airport,

01:26:55.470 --> 01:26:58.480
Takekawa was brought to the Ōsaka Police Security Department's Public Safety Division.

01:26:58.860 --> 01:27:03.040
We're thinking of bringing X there too once we reach Maizuru Harbour.

01:27:03.040 --> 01:27:04.950
You sure the Self-Defence Force doesn't have to be part of the investigation?

01:27:05.450 --> 01:27:08.810
There's no distinction between the JMSDF, the Coast Guard, or the Police when it comes to an investigation.

01:27:08.810 --> 01:27:11.730
Takekawa and X should be investigated together.

01:27:12.620 --> 01:27:14.040
I agree.

01:27:14.040 --> 01:27:14.780
Right.

01:27:16.980 --> 01:27:18.750
Now the case is closed!

01:27:18.750 --> 01:27:24.650
True. Looks like we didn't need your deductions this time, Mouri-<i>kun</i>.

01:27:29.830 --> 01:27:30.350
Mouri-<i>san</i>!

01:27:37.100 --> 01:27:37.940
Mouri-<i>san</i>?

01:27:37.940 --> 01:27:41.050
Umm, that's the captain's seat!

01:27:41.050 --> 01:27:41.900
Are you okay?

01:27:42.430 --> 01:27:45.360
No problem, I just felt slightly overcome.

01:27:45.920 --> 01:27:48.570
Seasickness? In a ship this big?

01:27:48.570 --> 01:27:52.540
No, I was overcome by the brilliance of my own deduction.

01:27:52.890 --> 01:27:55.540
What are you talking about now, Mouri-<i>kun</i>?

01:27:55.540 --> 01:27:57.000
I figured it out.

01:27:57.510 --> 01:27:59.960
I know who killed Sasaura-<i>san</i>.

01:28:00.320 --> 01:28:02.150
‘Who killed Sasaura-<i>san</i>’?

01:28:02.150 --> 01:28:04.420
Isn't it X, who we just arrested?

01:28:04.730 --> 01:28:10.380
X <i>did</i> infiltrate this boat to steal the data about the Aegis Destroyers.

01:28:10.380 --> 01:28:15.100
Yes. And he killed him in order to steal the data card in his phone.

01:28:15.450 --> 01:28:20.060
No, the person who stole the data card from his phone was Capt. Fujii.

01:28:21.040 --> 01:28:22.130
That's true.

01:28:22.130 --> 01:28:26.390
Huh? Then why was Sasaura-<i>san</i> murdered?

01:28:26.390 --> 01:28:29.030
Indeed, there was no reason for him to be killed.

01:28:29.460 --> 01:28:32.490
In other words, he wasn't killed by X!

01:28:32.490 --> 01:28:33.700
What?

01:28:34.060 --> 01:28:35.080
Then who...?

01:28:35.080 --> 01:28:37.060
Please think back.

01:28:37.060 --> 01:28:40.790
Sasaura-<i>san</i> was on a cliff at Maizuru Harbour this morning.

01:28:40.790 --> 01:28:43.050
Yes, waving a flag to X.

01:28:43.450 --> 01:28:47.010
Yes, and then he fell into the sea and died.

01:28:47.540 --> 01:28:52.220
In other words, he never boarded this ship today.

01:28:52.220 --> 01:28:53.450
Say what?

01:28:53.450 --> 01:28:55.890
But his phone was aboard this Aegis Destroyer!

01:28:55.890 --> 01:29:01.610
That's because the killer left it there in a hurry to make us think the victim had boarded this ship.

01:29:02.350 --> 01:29:04.570
Think back, Fujii-<i>san</i>.

01:29:05.660 --> 01:29:09.530
When and where did you find Sasaura-<i>san</i>'s phone?

01:29:10.180 --> 01:29:11.630
Now that you mention it...

01:29:11.630 --> 01:29:13.490
It was quite some time after we departed.

01:29:14.030 --> 01:29:19.040
And nobody noticed it before, despite being in such an obvious location.

01:29:19.040 --> 01:29:21.380
Exactly. So why?

01:29:21.380 --> 01:29:24.800
It's because it was a fake piece of evidence crafted after our departure.

01:29:25.490 --> 01:29:29.680
In other words, the killer is someone who boarded this Aegis Destroyer midway.

01:29:30.300 --> 01:29:32.720
Isn't that right, Kurata-<i>san</i>?

01:29:36.280 --> 01:29:38.180
Impossible!

01:29:38.180 --> 01:29:41.850
I hadn't even <i>heard</i> of Sasaura-<i>san</i> before this case!

01:29:41.850 --> 01:29:43.470
He's right, Mouri-<i>kun</i>!

01:29:43.470 --> 01:29:45.650
He had no motive to kill Sasaura-<i>san</i>!

01:29:45.650 --> 01:29:48.880
Yes, he didn't intend to kill him.

01:29:48.880 --> 01:29:49.750
What?!

01:29:49.750 --> 01:29:50.600
Conan!

01:29:50.600 --> 01:29:55.210
Play the voicemail recorded by Sasaura-<i>san</i> that we found on Takekawa-<i>san</i>'s phone.

01:29:55.910 --> 01:30:00.550
I saved the Aegis data on the KRY cloud. The access ID is...

01:30:00.550 --> 01:30:02.590
Can't you hear a metallic sound?

01:30:02.590 --> 01:30:03.340
You're right.

01:30:03.340 --> 01:30:05.200
I've heard that sound somewhere before...

01:30:05.200 --> 01:30:06.550
What is that sound?

01:30:06.910 --> 01:30:12.510
It's the sound made when an expandable baton and a gun secured at your waist bump into each other.

01:30:12.910 --> 01:30:15.100
Isn't that right, Kurata-<i>san</i>?

01:30:19.930 --> 01:30:21.440
Hold on!

01:30:21.440 --> 01:30:25.410
Everybody in the Security Department of the Coast Guard has an expandable baton and a gun!

01:30:25.410 --> 01:30:26.440
I see.

01:30:26.440 --> 01:30:30.300
But this voicemail was recorded this morning at 5:30.

01:30:30.300 --> 01:30:32.030
And his time of death is...

01:30:32.030 --> 01:30:33.990
This morning at 5:30!

01:30:35.210 --> 01:30:40.760
So he couldn't have boarded this ship while carrying his phone.

01:30:40.760 --> 01:30:47.420
Furthermore, you were the one who found the suspicious ship this morning at Maizuru Harbour, Kurata-<i>san</i>!

01:30:47.790 --> 01:30:51.510
So at that time, you were patrolling Maizuru Harbour.

01:30:52.060 --> 01:30:54.470
Or are you still going to deny it?

01:30:55.340 --> 01:30:56.380
Don't move!

01:31:00.810 --> 01:31:02.170
To think...

01:31:02.170 --> 01:31:06.190
I never thought things would turn out like this!

01:31:08.540 --> 01:31:09.860
Who could that be, this early?

01:31:11.000 --> 01:31:12.110
How strange...

01:31:13.450 --> 01:31:16.280
Hey! What are you doing there?!

01:31:17.160 --> 01:31:18.020
Damn...

01:31:23.910 --> 01:31:24.870
Hold on!

01:31:24.870 --> 01:31:26.330
This is the Coast Guard!

01:31:26.770 --> 01:31:28.580
Hey! Stop!

01:31:27.800 --> 01:31:29.290
He was obviously suspicious.

01:31:30.880 --> 01:31:32.090
Let me go!

01:31:42.560 --> 01:31:47.350
He was running away, having just conveyed the information about the Aegis Destroyers to Takekawa.

01:31:47.720 --> 01:31:49.690
I didn't know that.

01:31:50.040 --> 01:31:56.320
When I rushed to the bottom of the cliff to look for him in the sea, I found that suspicious ship.

01:31:56.640 --> 01:32:01.800
After that, I was busy reporting it to HQ and contacting the JMSDF.

01:32:04.020 --> 01:32:11.420
Then, at that time, we were informed by the Kyōto Police that Lt. Sasaura's arm had been found aboard this Aegis Destroyer.

01:32:11.830 --> 01:32:15.380
I quickly checked the belongings of this man who'd fallen this morning.

01:32:16.840 --> 01:32:22.400
And I realised that the man who'd been acting so suspiciously this morning was Lt. Sasaura.

01:32:24.540 --> 01:32:29.600
More than the charges for professional negligence, I was afraid of being charged with killing a Self-Defence Force member.

01:32:31.520 --> 01:32:36.450
So I asked my boss to let me
 take part in this investigation.

01:32:36.450 --> 01:32:37.740
Why did you do such a thing?

01:32:38.340 --> 01:32:41.990
It's because I knew there was a chance he'd been killed aboard this Aegis Destroyer.

01:32:42.440 --> 01:32:46.660
I thought that if he was found to be killed here, I could avoid facing my crime.

01:32:47.350 --> 01:32:51.880
So I pretended to be investigating, and put his phone in an obvious location on the deck.

01:32:52.340 --> 01:32:54.810
After that, you know the rest.

01:32:57.050 --> 01:33:05.190
I sincerely apologise for my selfish behaviour that disturbed the investigation.

01:33:13.730 --> 01:33:15.280
Uncle!

01:33:15.280 --> 01:33:16.690
Have you seen Ran anywhere?

01:33:16.690 --> 01:33:17.780
No.

01:33:17.780 --> 01:33:19.650
No matter how much we search, we can't find her!

01:33:20.120 --> 01:33:22.120
She probably got lost again.

01:33:22.120 --> 01:33:23.230
No!

01:33:23.230 --> 01:33:24.560
We looked everywhere!

01:33:24.560 --> 01:33:26.910
She disappeared after fighting the spy!

01:33:26.910 --> 01:33:28.310
What?!

01:33:28.310 --> 01:33:29.250
Inspector?

01:33:29.570 --> 01:33:30.950
What is it, Satō-<i>kun</i>?

01:33:30.950 --> 01:33:33.120
X made a rather alarming statement.

01:33:33.120 --> 01:33:34.340
An alarming statement?

01:33:34.340 --> 01:33:35.380
Yes.

01:33:35.380 --> 01:33:40.430
It seems his identity was exposed by a young lady just before we caught him.

01:33:40.430 --> 01:33:43.500
So he said he pushed her into the sea to keep her silent.

01:33:50.270 --> 01:33:55.150
It seems this young lady was of high school age and proficient in karate.

01:33:55.150 --> 01:33:56.260
Karate?

01:33:56.260 --> 01:33:57.230
Could it be?

01:33:57.230 --> 01:33:58.440
R-Ran!

01:33:58.440 --> 01:33:59.450
No way!

01:33:59.450 --> 01:34:00.950
No way! Ran-<i>san</i>...

01:34:00.950 --> 01:34:01.700
No!

01:34:02.900 --> 01:34:03.710
Don't tell me...

01:34:04.280 --> 01:34:05.370
Ran!

01:34:18.110 --> 01:34:20.800
Please hold onto any nearby handrails or tables you can find.

01:34:20.800 --> 01:34:23.680
Make sure to hold onto your children.

01:34:31.530 --> 01:34:36.310
According to X's statement, Mouri-<i>san</i> fell overboard around here.

01:34:36.310 --> 01:34:38.580
We're pretty far away.

01:34:38.580 --> 01:34:40.230
Wait!

01:34:40.230 --> 01:34:40.950
It's fine!

01:34:40.950 --> 01:34:43.120
Anyway, get the patrol helicopter ready!

01:34:43.120 --> 01:34:43.930
Roger!

01:34:43.930 --> 01:34:45.200
Move!

01:34:45.200 --> 01:34:46.740
I made some calculations based on the tides.

01:34:47.370 --> 01:34:48.660
She should be in this area.

01:34:48.660 --> 01:34:49.980
No way...

01:34:49.980 --> 01:34:51.870
It's four times bigger than usual!

01:34:51.870 --> 01:34:56.130
Because of the low pressure coming from the southwest, the ocean currents are faster than usual.

01:34:56.130 --> 01:34:58.360
The waves are starting to get rougher too.

01:34:58.360 --> 01:35:02.340
Considering the stamina of the victim, every second counts...

01:35:02.340 --> 01:35:04.520
Patrol helicopter ready!

01:35:04.520 --> 01:35:06.550
All right. Depart right away!

01:35:06.550 --> 01:35:06.800
Yes, sir!

01:35:06.800 --> 01:35:07.850
Let me get in too!

01:35:08.900 --> 01:35:10.500
Don't be stupid!

01:35:10.500 --> 01:35:11.040
But...

01:35:11.040 --> 01:35:13.310
A kid would just be a hindrance!

01:35:14.020 --> 01:35:15.270
Damn it...

01:35:28.030 --> 01:35:31.850
Considering the stamina of the victim, every second counts.

01:35:31.850 --> 01:35:34.250
We have to find her before sunset no matter what!

01:35:34.250 --> 01:35:35.710
Roger.

01:35:35.710 --> 01:35:37.690
Every second counts?

01:35:37.690 --> 01:35:38.520
Ran...

01:35:38.520 --> 01:35:40.400
Ran will be okay, won't she?

01:35:43.010 --> 01:35:45.680
What happens when somebody falls from that deck?

01:35:45.680 --> 01:35:48.890
She should be wearing her lifejacket,

01:35:48.890 --> 01:35:51.930
but that's all she would have. 
If she fell in the wrong place...

01:35:51.930 --> 01:35:53.020
How...

01:35:53.020 --> 01:35:55.730
Of course, there's still hope.

01:36:00.240 --> 01:36:00.990
Ran-<i>san</i>!

01:36:00.990 --> 01:36:01.940
No!

01:36:03.700 --> 01:36:07.460
Miss... It's all my fault!

01:36:08.700 --> 01:36:12.000
Don't we have any way to guarantee her safety?

01:36:12.000 --> 01:36:14.580
All we can do now is leave it to the patrol helicopter.

01:36:15.370 --> 01:36:21.210
Damn it, even if we reduce the search field, it's nearly impossible to check the whole area before sunset.

01:36:21.210 --> 01:36:25.130
Besides, Ran might still be drifting on the waves...!

01:36:26.760 --> 01:36:31.000
Save me... Shin'ichi!

01:36:33.890 --> 01:36:37.140
We're on location. We're beginning the search.

01:36:37.450 --> 01:36:39.000
I'll call for her through the speaker.

01:36:39.000 --> 01:36:40.280
Plug me in.

01:36:40.280 --> 01:36:40.610
OK!

01:36:41.610 --> 01:36:42.850
Mouri-<i>san</i>!

01:36:42.850 --> 01:36:44.220
Ran Mouri-<i>san</i>!

01:36:44.220 --> 01:36:45.940
We came to rescue you!

01:36:45.940 --> 01:36:47.560
We're going to save you!

01:36:47.560 --> 01:36:49.550
Hold on a little bit longer!

01:36:49.550 --> 01:36:50.140
Ran!

01:36:50.140 --> 01:36:51.030
Ran, where are you?

01:36:51.030 --> 01:36:51.990
Ran!

01:36:51.990 --> 01:36:53.760
Hold on just a little!

01:36:53.760 --> 01:36:54.470
Miss!

01:36:54.470 --> 01:36:54.980
Don't die!

01:36:54.980 --> 01:36:56.540
We'll save you soon!

01:36:56.910 --> 01:37:00.970
I gotta calm down! There still
 has to be a way to find Ran.

01:37:00.970 --> 01:37:02.750
The waves are getting even faster.

01:37:03.100 --> 01:37:05.460
I think we need to enlarge the search field.

01:37:05.460 --> 01:37:07.070
We don't have any time left before sunset.

01:37:07.070 --> 01:37:10.840
Limit the search to the Alpha Bravo Fox area and keep on searching!

01:37:11.150 --> 01:37:13.630
Roger! Heading for the Alpha Bravo Fox area!

01:37:29.430 --> 01:37:31.610
Ran Mouri-<i>san</i>, we came to rescue you.

01:37:31.610 --> 01:37:33.580
Hold on just a little bit longer!

01:37:33.580 --> 01:37:35.800
It's got a lot darker.

01:37:36.750 --> 01:37:39.090
There's less than 15 minutes before sunset.

01:37:40.960 --> 01:37:42.040
Sunset...

01:37:43.110 --> 01:37:44.200
Sunset?!

01:37:44.200 --> 01:37:45.170
Why does that matter?!

01:37:45.760 --> 01:37:50.380
Keep on looking! Keep on looking until you find her!

01:37:51.250 --> 01:37:53.530
I wish we could...

01:37:53.530 --> 01:37:59.100
But in this season, the water temperature drops suddenly just before sunset, at 5 PM.

01:37:59.570 --> 01:38:01.800
So even if we find her after 5 PM...

01:38:02.810 --> 01:38:03.750
That's enough, Kishi-<i>san</i>!

01:38:02.810 --> 01:38:06.150
Oh, no! The water temperature might already be dropping.

01:38:03.750 --> 01:38:08.360
I'm sorry, miss. A rescue squad are heading here now, and we would best off leaving the rest of the search to them...

01:38:06.450 --> 01:38:08.360
Damn, we don't have time!

01:38:08.730 --> 01:38:10.870
Isn't there any way to find her?

01:38:12.430 --> 01:38:13.030
Watch?

01:38:14.880 --> 01:38:17.380
Oh, yeah, Ran has Mitsuhiko's watch.

01:38:17.380 --> 01:38:18.450
Why?!

01:38:19.270 --> 01:38:20.950
Why are you going to stop looking for her?

01:38:20.950 --> 01:38:22.700
We will find her!

01:38:22.700 --> 01:38:23.670
So don't give up!

01:38:23.990 --> 01:38:25.850
This ship's supposed to be incredible!

01:38:25.850 --> 01:38:26.390
Yes!

01:38:26.390 --> 01:38:27.450
Do something!

01:38:27.450 --> 01:38:29.340
It's the great detective of the seas, right?

01:38:30.610 --> 01:38:31.760
The great detective of the seas?

01:38:34.590 --> 01:38:37.720
I see. If we use the radar on this Aegis Destroyer...

01:38:39.070 --> 01:38:45.100
At 1700 hours, we will leave the victim rescue to the specialist squad, and head back to Maizuru Harbour.

01:38:45.100 --> 01:38:47.200
The radio watch!

01:38:47.200 --> 01:38:49.030
Ran has a radio watch!

01:38:49.490 --> 01:38:52.500
This Aegis Destroyer should be able to pick up that radio signal, right?

01:38:52.500 --> 01:38:55.280
Mitsuhiko! You said the watch was fully waterproof, right?

01:38:55.990 --> 01:38:56.450
Right!

01:38:57.030 --> 01:38:59.830
The watch sends signals at 5 AM and PM sharp!

01:39:00.310 --> 01:39:01.290
Captain, we don't have time!

01:39:01.290 --> 01:39:02.950
Hurry up!

01:39:02.950 --> 01:39:04.970
Prepare the radio wave radar immediately!

01:39:07.150 --> 01:39:11.100
1 minute 40 seconds left until 5 PM. Can we do it?

01:39:11.100 --> 01:39:12.130
We have to try!

01:39:13.900 --> 01:39:15.840
Alert the bridge and the deck! Quickly!

01:39:13.900 --> 01:39:15.840
Start the radio wave radar!

01:39:15.840 --> 01:39:17.800
This is not a drill.

01:39:17.800 --> 01:39:20.270
I repeat, this is not a drill.

01:39:20.270 --> 01:39:22.300
Everyone on deck must evacuate urgently!

01:39:22.300 --> 01:39:25.480
I repeat, everyone on deck must evacuate urgently!

01:39:24.950 --> 01:39:25.480
Evacuate!

01:39:27.150 --> 01:39:28.240
Please, make it in time!

01:39:28.240 --> 01:39:29.020
Evacuation done!

01:39:29.380 --> 01:39:32.160
Radio wave radar ready!

01:39:32.160 --> 01:39:33.860
Start the ES search.

01:39:33.860 --> 01:39:35.150
Search started!

01:39:35.520 --> 01:39:39.400
It is currently 1659 hours. Only
 10 seconds remaining until 5 PM.

01:39:40.330 --> 01:39:41.290
9...

01:39:41.290 --> 01:39:42.250
8...

01:39:42.250 --> 01:39:43.200
7...

01:39:43.200 --> 01:39:44.160
6...

01:39:44.160 --> 01:39:45.120
5...

01:39:45.120 --> 01:39:46.160
4...

01:39:46.160 --> 01:39:47.100
3...

01:39:47.100 --> 01:39:48.040
2...

01:39:48.040 --> 01:39:49.000
1...

01:39:49.780 --> 01:39:50.340
Now!

01:40:02.750 --> 01:40:03.390
Any response?

01:40:04.750 --> 01:40:07.850
No response within the search range...

01:40:10.360 --> 01:40:11.650
No way... How?!

01:40:11.650 --> 01:40:18.550
Maybe her radio watch has
 already sunk deep into the sea...

01:40:20.510 --> 01:40:21.210
Ran...

01:40:33.840 --> 01:40:34.510
It can't be...

01:40:34.510 --> 01:40:35.890
This...

01:40:35.890 --> 01:40:36.700
...can't be...

01:40:36.700 --> 01:40:38.280
You'll always manage to find me, right?

01:40:40.850 --> 01:40:43.530
That's why I said I'd come with you.

01:40:43.530 --> 01:40:44.310
But...

01:40:45.050 --> 01:40:47.150
Don't go wandering off by yourself again, okay?

01:40:47.780 --> 01:40:50.440
Next time, you mightn't be able to find me.

01:40:50.440 --> 01:40:51.290
It's fine.

01:40:52.580 --> 01:40:55.780
No matter how lost I am, you'll 
always manage to find me, right?

01:40:57.290 --> 01:41:00.030
You're a great detective, after all!

01:41:05.460 --> 01:41:09.500
How can I be a great detective... I can't even find Ran!

01:41:10.690 --> 01:41:11.460
Ran...

01:41:12.470 --> 01:41:12.990
Ran...

01:41:13.950 --> 01:41:14.690
Ran...

01:41:15.380 --> 01:41:16.840
Ran...

01:41:17.340 --> 01:41:18.300
Ran...

01:41:24.310 --> 01:41:28.840
Ran!

01:41:35.120 --> 01:41:37.650
Just now... That was Conan-<i>kun</i>'s voice...

01:41:39.480 --> 01:41:43.410
Didn't I tell you? I'll always find you, no matter what.

01:41:44.000 --> 01:41:45.880
You're late!

01:41:47.700 --> 01:41:49.810
Shin'ichi!

01:41:55.390 --> 01:41:55.750
Could it be?

01:41:58.370 --> 01:42:00.960
It's very weak, but I'm detecting radio waves!

01:42:00.960 --> 01:42:02.050
They're getting stronger and stronger!

01:42:03.040 --> 01:42:03.800
It's Ran!

01:42:04.100 --> 01:42:05.140
Ran is there!

01:42:05.140 --> 01:42:06.710
Lead the helicopter there!

01:42:08.120 --> 01:42:10.140
Lead the patrol helicopter there!

01:42:10.140 --> 01:42:11.330
Roger!

01:42:11.330 --> 01:42:14.060
Target coordinates are four kilometres northwest of the destroyer.

01:42:14.060 --> 01:42:15.510
Latitude 36°4'.

01:42:15.510 --> 01:42:16.940
Longitude 135°.

01:42:16.940 --> 01:42:19.650
SH, hurry towards the point.

01:42:19.650 --> 01:42:21.930
Roger. Heading towards the point.

01:42:26.170 --> 01:42:28.200
We'll be arriving at the search point soon.

01:42:32.900 --> 01:42:35.130
We're straight above the search point but visibility is low.

01:42:35.790 --> 01:42:37.840
The reflection of the setting sun on the waves is hindering our view.

01:42:38.350 --> 01:42:40.800
Finding someone in these conditions will be hard...

01:42:39.050 --> 01:42:39.850
Reflection?

01:42:40.800 --> 01:42:45.560
Hey, that reflection — is there a
 single spot that's glittering a lot?

01:42:46.470 --> 01:42:47.020
Umm...

01:42:47.020 --> 01:42:49.170
Well? Please answer.

01:42:49.170 --> 01:42:54.750
Yes. Part of the sea is strangely glittering and reflecting light from the helicopter.

01:42:54.750 --> 01:42:55.740
There!

01:42:55.740 --> 01:42:56.560
Follow those lights!

01:42:57.140 --> 01:42:58.780
Ran should be at their source!

01:42:59.710 --> 01:43:02.800
Ask the helicopter to head there as the kid said!

01:43:02.800 --> 01:43:04.210
Please, Captain!

01:43:06.010 --> 01:43:07.490
Follow the bright, floating objects.

01:43:07.900 --> 01:43:10.480
We believe the victim is where those objects concentrate.

01:43:10.480 --> 01:43:10.950
Roger.

01:43:27.490 --> 01:43:30.010
We've reached the location where the floating objects are concentrated.

01:43:30.490 --> 01:43:31.720
We're descending now!

01:43:34.770 --> 01:43:35.920
There's something directly beneath us!

01:43:38.860 --> 01:43:41.190
It's clearly not one of the floating objects.

01:43:44.660 --> 01:43:45.300
Found her!

01:43:45.910 --> 01:43:46.780
We found the victim!

01:43:47.690 --> 01:43:48.980
We can confirm she's alive!

01:43:48.980 --> 01:43:50.740
We're starting the rescue!

01:43:53.140 --> 01:43:54.580
All right!

01:43:55.510 --> 01:43:56.900
We did it, Takagi-<i>kun</i>!

01:43:57.470 --> 01:43:58.130
Satō-<i>san</i>...

01:43:59.940 --> 01:44:04.800
Good work. You did well. Take her to the hospital as soon as you pick her up.

01:44:04.800 --> 01:44:06.140
Roger.

01:44:06.140 --> 01:44:08.100
It seems the victim is still conscious.

01:44:08.100 --> 01:44:10.010
But we'll take her to the hospital just in case.

01:44:10.540 --> 01:44:13.470
Her body temperature appears to be low, but her heartbeat is stable.

01:44:15.250 --> 01:44:16.750
Shin'ichi...

01:44:21.480 --> 01:44:22.360
Old man...

01:44:24.500 --> 01:44:25.260
Thank you!

01:44:41.670 --> 01:44:56.020
Last night, I dreamt about when we were still young

01:44:41.670 --> 01:44:56.020
Last night, I dreamt about when we were still young

